{
  "raw": {
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327100": {
      "title": "Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Microbiology and Immunology - 422501 Posting Open Date 10/15/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Vacancy ID PDS005001 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on experience and/or qualifications Proposed Start Date 12/01/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Cameron-Arnold laboratory in the Department of Microbiology and Immunology at the University of North Carolina School of Medicine in Chapel Hill, NC, is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral research associate to investigate the biochemical and biophysical mechanisms of RNA virus genome replication. Our laboratory has established, NIH -supported research programs focused on the enzymology of RNA -dependent RNA polymerases, viral ATPases and helicases, and the protein complexes responsible for genome replication in picornaviruses, alphaviruses, and coronaviruses. Research will focus on defining the molecular mechanisms of viral RNA synthesis, including initiation, elongation, nucleotide selection, fidelity, RNA recombination, and the regulation of viral replication machinery. Additional areas of investigation include the kinetic mechanisms of viral ATPases and helicases, the assembly and function of multiprotein replication complexes, coronavirus RNA proofreading and transcription, and the biochemical mechanisms of antiviral drug action and resistance. These studies employ a combination of quantitative enzymology, protein biochemistry, molecular biophysics, and complementary structural and cellular approaches. The successful candidate will develop and pursue mechanistic research projects within the laboratory’s established areas of investigation. Our overarching goal is to establish a quantitative understanding of the molecular mechanisms governing RNA virus genome replication and to use this knowledge to identify opportunities for antiviral therapeutic development. The position offers extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, development of advanced biochemical and biophysical expertise, scientific publication, and preparation for an independent research career. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in Biochemistry, Biophysics, Chemistry, Molecular Biology, or a closely related discipline. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience PhD in Biochemistry, Biophysics, Chemistry, Molecular Biology, or a closely related discipline. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Prior research experience in protein biochemistry, enzymology, molecular biophysics, or mechanistic studies of protein-nucleic acid interactions. Experience with recombinant protein expression and purification, quantitative enzyme kinetics, fluorescence spectroscopy, nucleic acid biochemistry, or biophysical characterization of macromolecular complexes is desirable. Experience with pre-steady-state kinetics or viral replication proteins would be particularly valuable but is not required. Candidates demonstrating strong quantitative and analytical skills, scientific curiosity, effective communication skills, and the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327097 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Peyton Dabbs Department Contact Telephone or Email peyton_dabbs@med.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327099": {
      "title": "Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Microbiology and Immunology - 422501 Posting Open Date 10/15/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Research Associate - Cameron/Arnold Lab Vacancy ID PDS005000 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on experience and/or qualifications Proposed Start Date 12/01/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Cameron-Arnold laboratory in the Department of Microbiology and Immunology at the University of North Carolina School of Medicine in Chapel Hill, NC, is seeking a highly motivated postdoctoral research associate to investigate the molecular and cellular mechanisms of RNA virus genome replication. Our laboratory has established research programs supported by the National Institutes of Health that focus on picornaviruses, alphaviruses, and coronaviruses. These programs seek to understand how viral and host proteins coordinate viral RNA synthesis, replication-complex assembly, genome maintenance, and virus multiplication. Research will integrate molecular biology, cell biology, genetics, and virology to investigate the mechanisms governing viral genome replication and the interactions between viral replication machinery and the host cell. Areas of investigation include the regulation of genomic and subgenomic RNA synthesis, formation and function of membrane-associated replication complexes, viral RNA recombination, and the contributions of viral and host factors to genome replication and virus assembly. These studies will complement ongoing biochemical and biophysical investigations of viral replication proteins and macromolecular complexes. The successful candidate will develop and pursue research projects within the laboratory’s established areas of investigation, working collaboratively with faculty, postdoctoral researchers, graduate students, and scientific staff. Our overarching objective is to advance fundamental knowledge of RNA virus replication and identify mechanisms that may be exploited for antiviral therapeutic development. The position provides opportunities for scientific independence, interdisciplinary collaboration, publication, and professional development in preparation for an independent research career. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in Microbiology, Virology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Biochemistry, or a closely related discipline. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience PhD in Microbiology, Virology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Biochemistry, or a closely related discipline. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Prior research experience in molecular virology, molecular and cellular biology, or RNA biology. Experience with mammalian cell culture, molecular cloning, viral replicon systems, quantitative RNA analysis, fluorescence microscopy, or cell-based studies of virus replication is desirable. Candidates demonstrating strong experimental skills, scientific curiosity, effective communication skills, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327096 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Peyton Dabbs Department Contact Telephone or Email Peyton_Dabbs@med.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327086": {
      "title": "Faculty Physician / Clinician Educator (Chatham Hospital)",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Faculty Physician / Clinician Educator (Chatham Hospital) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Faculty Physician / Clinician Educator (Chatham Hospital) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Family Medicine - 411601 Posting Open Date 08/12/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Faculty Physician / Clinician Educator (Chatham Hospital) Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006053 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week TBD FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and Qualifications Proposed Start Date 11/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Family Medicine at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, in partnership with UNC Health and Chatham Hospital, seeks a Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine Physician for the UNC Chatham Hospital Emergency Department. UNC Chatham Hospital is a 25-bed rural Critical Access Hospital located in Siler City, NC, approximately 30 miles from Chapel Hill. The newly renovated 15-bed ED sees approximately 18,000 visits annually and is staffed by Family Medicine and Emergency Medicine physicians and advanced practice providers. This is an excellent opportunity to join a diverse and energetic group of physicians providing emergency care to a rural community. The ED team is supported by advanced practice providers, telepsychiatry services, on-site interpreter services, a system transfer center, and UNC AirCare. We use Epic as our EHR with AI-powered documentation support. CT and ultrasound are available daily, with MRI available five days per week. Bedside ultrasound and GlideScope are also available. The Maternity Care Center is staffed 24/7 with cesarean section capability, and cardiology and general surgery consultants are readily available. Physicians in the ED practice group are employed through the UNC Department of Family Medicine, consistently ranked a top academic family medicine program in the United States. Our mission is to provide outstanding, compassionate health care to the surrounding rural community. The ED serves as a training site for medical students, residents, and fellows. Faculty interested in academic advancement have opportunities for professional development across the department’s missions, including teaching, clinical excellence, research, and administration. The position offers flexible scheduling options with a mix of day, evening, and overnight shifts. Full-time equivalent is 1520 hours annually. The manageable patient volume allows for meaningful patient interactions while maintaining work-life balance in a collegial, team-based environment. Faculty rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications and experience. The position includes excellent UNC faculty physician benefits and clinical incentive pay. Benefits include: Competitive salary with clinical incentive compensation Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance Generous retirement contributions ( UNC system) Paid time off and CME allowance Professional liability coverage Opportunities for academic advancement Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or DO required. Candidates must be board eligible or board certified in Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine. Current certifications in ACLS , PALS , and ATLS will be required. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Clinical experience in an emergency department setting, rural practice, and teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/323846 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Jaime Adams, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email jfadams@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other * Do you hold a MD or DO? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked in an emergency room setting? - If so, in what capacity? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327084": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Radiology - Abdominal Imaging - 412813 Posting Open Date 05/26/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005949 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 11/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary Flexible work arrangements, including virtual and hybrid work locations, are an integral part of the School of Medicine’s Working Forward initiative. This position may be eligible for a virtual or hybrid work arrangement, in accordance with UNC policy and subject to approval based on the unit’s business needs. Please note that the approved work location may change over time to meet operational requirements. Position Description The Department of Radiology at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking an Abdominal Imaging Radiologist to join the Abdominal Imaging Division. This position supports the department’s clinical, educational, and academic missions within a high volume academic medical center. The Abdominal Imaging Division provides diagnostic imaging services across the UNC Hospitals system, including a Level I Trauma Center, Women’s Hospital, Children’s Hospital, Neurosciences Hospital, and the NCI designated Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Center. Faculty collaborate closely with multidisciplinary clinical teams to support comprehensive patient care. Position Responsibilities Interpret a full range of abdominal imaging studies, including CT, MRI , ultrasound, radiographs, and fluoroscopy Participate in teaching and mentoring diagnostic radiology residents, fellows, and medical students Collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical teams through conferences, consultations, and protocol development Participate in departmental, divisional, and institutional quality improvement initiatives Engage in scholarly or research activities consistent with departmental needs Appointment Details This is an open rank, fixed term faculty appointment at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Board certified or board eligible Radiologist Fellowship training in Abdominal Imaging or equivalent clinical experience Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary clinical teams Interest or experience in resident and fellow education in an academic medical setting Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319608 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Alexis Evans, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email alexis_evans@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
