    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327068": {
      "title": "Comprehensive Ophthalmologist (Open Rank Faculty)",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Comprehensive Ophthalmologist (Open Rank Faculty) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Comprehensive Ophthalmologist (Open Rank Faculty) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Anyone wishing to be considered for the position should submit a formal application at the following link ( https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247109 ) in addition to a full CV, cover letter, and list of 3-5 professional contacts who may be reached to provide a written letter of reference for candidacy. Posting Information Posting Information Department Ophthalmology - OphthCarCr - 413249 Posting Open Date 12/21/2022 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Comprehensive Ophthalmologist (Open Rank Faculty) Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0004385 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Qualifications Proposed Start Date 09/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC School of Medicine has a rich tradition of excellence and care. Our mission is to improve the health and wellbeing of North Carolinians, and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. We strive to promote faculty, staff, and learner development in a diverse, respectful environment where our colleagues demonstrate professionalism, enhance learning, and create personal and professional sustainability. We optimize our partnership with the UNC Health System through close collaboration and commitment to service. OUR VISION Our vision is to be the nation’s leading public school of medicine. We are ranked 2nd in primary care education among all US schools of medicine and 5th among public peers in NIH research funding. Our Allied Health Department is home to five top-ranked divisions, and we are home to 18 top-ranked clinical and basic science departments in NIH research funding. OUR MISSION Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. Patient Care: We will promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We will prepare tomorrow’s health care professionals and biomedical researchers by facilitating learning within innovative curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education. We will cultivate outstanding teaching and research faculty, and we will recruit outstanding students and trainees from highly diverse backgrounds to create a socially responsible, highly skilled workforce. Research: We will develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers, and resources. We will provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our University to support outstanding research. We will foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic, and population research. Position Summary An open rank, fixed-term Comprehensive Ophthalmologist position is currently available in the Department of Ophthalmology at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. Responsibilities include a strong commitment to clinical, resident teaching and supervision as well as medical student teaching. Rank and salary are commensurate with experience. This position will report directly to the new Chair of the Department of Ophthalmology, Dr. Benjamin Frankfort. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Prerequisites include successful completion of an approved residency in Ophthalmology and demonstration of excellence in all scholarly and training activities. Qualifications include board certification or eligibility, and eligibility for licensure in North Carolina. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Qualifications include board certification or eligibility, and eligibility for licensure in North Carolina. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Anyone wishing to be considered for the position should submit a formal application at the following link ( https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247109 ) in addition to a full CV, cover letter, and list of 3-5 professional contacts who may be reached to provide a written letter of reference for candidacy. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247109 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Gina Austen, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email gina_austen@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327063": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Neuromuscular Control and Biomechanics",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor - Neuromuscular Control and Biomechanics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Assistant Professor - Neuromuscular Control and Biomechanics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The application should include the following: 1) letter of application, 2) a Research Statement (no more than 3 pages) highlighting the applicant’s previous and ongoing research, plans for future innovation, and potential collaborators, 3) a Teaching Statement (no more than 2 pages) describing the candidate’s teaching philosophy, potential classes to teach and/or develop, and experiences mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and 4) complete academic curriculum vitae . Applicants are also required to identify the names, titles/positions, email addresses, and phone numbers of four (4) professional references who may be contacted with instructions for submitting recommendation letters. For additional information, please contact Dr. Brian Pietrosimone, Search Committee Chair, at brian@unc.edu . Deadline: Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, and will close on November 25, 2026 Posting Information Posting Information Department Exercise and Sport Science - 318600 Posting Open Date 10/15/2026 Application Deadline 11/25/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Assistant Professor - Neuromuscular Control and Biomechanics Appointment Type Tenured/Tenure Track Vacancy ID FAC0006167 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Salary commensurate with experience Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is a major research university in the University of North Carolina System with student enrollment exceeding 29,000 students. The Department of Exercise and Sport Science (exss.unc.edu) supports an undergraduate program of over 1,400 undergraduate majors with three specialization areas (Exercise and Sport Science, Fitness Professional, Sport Administration); a Master of Arts graduate program enrolling ~60 students also with three specializations (Exercise Physiology, Kinesiology, Sport Administration); and a doctoral program in Human Movement Science in partnership with the UNC -CH School of Medicine (hmsc.unc.edu). The mission of the Department of Exercise and Sport Science ( EXSS ) is to discover, create and promote knowledge of human movement to improve the quality of life of individuals and society. The mission of EXSS is further enhanced through interdisciplinary cooperation and departmental faculty securing competitive extramural funding in the form of contracts and grants. These endeavors enable the department to advance knowledge and thus serve the state and nation. The teaching, research, and service efforts of the EXSS Department are supported by an outstanding faculty and staff, which currently includes: 39 full-time faculty, 9 part-time (fixed term) faculty, 20 joint appointment/ adjunct faculty, 8 emeritus faculty, and 27 full-time EXSS staff members. Position Summary The Department of Exercise and Sport Science invites applications for a 9-month tenure track Assistant Professor faculty position to deepen and expand research in any area of neuromuscular control and biomechanics while teaching in areas related to exercise and sport science, biomechanics, and/or motor control. We aspire to recruit faculty engaged in innovative and highly impactful scholarship that will diversify and enhance our research, teaching, and public outreach missions, and who can translate this research to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in biomechanics, neuromuscular control, motor control, and/or sports medicine. This position assumes a lead research role within the Department of Exercise and Sport Science within the College of Arts and Sciences. Successful candidates will demonstrate expertise in neuromuscular control and biomechanics which may involve, but not be limited to, musculoskeletal health outcomes, mechanisms related to biomechanical and/ or neuromuscular disease, neurotrauma, and/or promoting healthy movement and performance. The individual is expected to possess expertise in their chosen neuromuscular control and biomechanics field, which may include biomechanical assessments, measurement, and analysis. Potential applicants should have a strong interest in developing impactful collaborative opportunities within the Department, across the College of Arts and Sciences, and across the greater UNC community (including the nationally ranked School of Medicine and Gillings School of Global Public Health, Human Science Curriculum and Department of Biomedical Engineering). Applicants should have a record of scholarly productivity and interdisciplinary research. The interest areas of the applicant should align with and complement the faculty affiliated with the Department of Exercise and Sport Science that are collecting neuromuscular control and biomechanics data including MOTION Science Institute, UNC Sports Medicine Institute, STAR HEEL Laboratory and/or the Matthew Gfeller Center. Responsibilities: * Plan, establish, and develop a focused independent research agenda, with preference for applicants who demonstrate a significant publication record and demonstrate a record of extramural grant submission * Seek extramural funding to support research efforts * Collaborate with colleagues across campus and in Exercise and Sport Science to support and develop multidisciplinary research projects * Serve as a mentor to undergraduate and graduate students across a diverse student population * Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Exercise and Sport Science related to biomechanics, neuromuscular control, motor control, sports medicine and/or other classes aligning with the candidate’s expertise as requested by the department Chair * Serve as a research advisor and/or committee member for undergraduate and graduate students in the Department of Exercise and Sport Science * Participate as a core faculty member and contribute to mentoring doctoral trainees in the Human Movement Science doctoral program * Perform other responsibilities and duties as may be assigned by the Department Chair Minimum Education and Experience Requirements All candidates must have an earned doctorate (or terminal degree) in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Engineering, Neuroscience, Motor Control, Sports Medicine, or related field with demonstrated expertise in neuromuscular control and biomechanics. Record of research publications is required and a record of, or strong potential for, securing extramural research funding and/or currently working on extramurally funded projects. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience * Experience mentoring students is preferred * Collegiate-level teaching experience is preferred Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions The application should include the following: 1) letter of application, 2) a Research Statement (no more than 3 pages) highlighting the applicant’s previous and ongoing research, plans for future innovation, and potential collaborators, 3) a Teaching Statement (no more than 2 pages) describing the candidate’s teaching philosophy, potential classes to teach and/or develop, and experiences mentoring undergraduate and graduate students, and 4) complete academic curriculum vitae . Applicants are also required to identify the names, titles/positions, email addresses, and phone numbers of four (4) professional references who may be contacted with instructions for submitting recommendation letters. For additional information, please contact Dr. Brian Pietrosimone, Search Committee Chair, at brian@unc.edu . Deadline: Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026, and will close on November 25, 2026 Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326914 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Dr. Brian Pietrosimone, Search Committee Chair Department Contact Telephone or Email brian@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327060": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in School Counseling (Open Rank — Fixed Term/Clinical or Teaching)",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Faculty Position in School Counseling (Open Rank — Fixed Term/Clinical or Teaching) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Faculty Position in School Counseling (Open Rank — Fixed Term/Clinical or Teaching) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply for the position, submit a letter of interest, vita, and the names of four references with full contact information, using the online application process at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326737 . For full consideration, all application materials should be received by December 1, 2026, at which time the search committee begins reviewing applications. The search will remain open until it is filled. For more information, email the Search Chair, Dr. Joseph Williams, at jmwill@unc.edu . Posting Information Posting Information Department SOE Academic - 340200 Posting Open Date 10/09/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Faculty Position in School Counseling (Open Rank — Fixed Term/Clinical or Teaching) Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006160 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. The UNC School of Education , one of the longest-standing professional schools at the nation’s first public university, ranks among the top schools of education in the U.S. and offers a full range of degree programs, from undergraduate to doctorate; forward-thinking certificate and licensure programs; and in-person, online, and HyFlex offerings. Faculty members generate knowledge across a number of fields, including human development, educational technology and entrepreneurship, teaching and learning, school counseling, school psychology, administration, educational policy and leadership, and more; they also prepare students to become the most highly effective educators to lead in classrooms, schools, districts and beyond, as well as future scholars and researchers. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill (Carolina), established in 1793 as the first public university in the nation, is a doctoral-granting institution situated in the beautiful college town of Chapel Hill, NC. Ranked fifth among public institutions by US News & World Report, and one of the original public ivy schools, Carolina has earned a reputation as one of the best universities in the world. We pride ourselves on a strong, diverse student body, unparalleled academic opportunities, and a value unmatched by any public university in the nation. In 2026, the School of Education ranked No. 32 overall and No. 28 among public schools of education. In the most recent ranking of school counseling programs by U.S. News & World Report, in 2025, Carolina’s School Counseling program ranked No. 13. The School of Education is an academic unit reporting to the Provost. The School is a major center of research, teaching, and public service within the State of North Carolina, the nation, and the world. The School offers a full range of undergraduate and graduate programs. The mission of the School of Education is to conduct research, and generate basic and applied knowledge about human development, educational technology and entrepreneurship, teaching and learning, school counseling, school psychology, administration, as well as educational policy and leadership; prepare leaders in the profession of education by conducting outstanding research, teaching, and service; and assist in the development of strong and effective public schools in North Carolina. In order to fulfill its mission, the School is organized into three academic divisions: (1) Culture, Curriculum, & Teacher Education ( CCATE ), (2) Learning, Development & Psychological Sciences ( LDPS ), and (3) Educational Policy, Organization, & Leadership ( EPOL ). Position Summary The School of Education at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill invites applications for a faculty position in School Counseling at the rank of Clinical Assistant, Clinical Associate, or Clinical Professor, starting July 1, 2027. UNC’s nationally recognized CACREP -accredited School Counseling program prepares culturally responsive school counselors through rigorous coursework, immersive school-based fieldwork, and individualized professional mentorship. We seek candidates with professional experience in school counseling and a passion for preparing future counselors. This full-time, 9-month position is for a three-year term, with the potential to renew for additional terms, and will include undergraduate and graduate teaching and supervision, student mentoring, and program leadership. Candidates will: a) teach undergraduate courses in Human Development and Family Sciences as well as graduate courses in the School Counseling program in face to face, online, and/or blended formats, including fieldwork supervision courses; b) serve as the program’s Clinical and Admissions Coordinator, providing program-level leadership for recruitment, admissions, and practicum and internship coordination in collaboration with School of Education faculty and staff; and c) provide advising, mentoring, and other supports to students. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Candidates must have an earned doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP accredited program. Candidates must also have practical experience as a school counselor (license eligible in NC). Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated excellence in teaching and counselor preparation, including the ability to teach across the counselor education core and experience with clinical supervision, student advising and mentoring, program coordination, recruitment and admissions, and knowledge of CACREP standards and requirements. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions To apply for the position, submit a letter of interest, vita, and the names of four references with full contact information, using the online application process at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326737 . For full consideration, all application materials should be received by December 1, 2026, at which time the search committee begins reviewing applications. The search will remain open until it is filled. For more information, email the Search Chair, Dr. Joseph Williams, at jmwill@unc.edu . Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326737 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Joseph Williams, Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email jmwill@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327059": {
      "title": "Division Chief - Division of Hospital Medicine",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Division Chief - Division of Hospital Medicine Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Division Chief - Division of Hospital Medicine Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required Documents: Curriculum vitae, cover letter Posting Information Posting Information Department Medicine Hospitalist - 411404 Posting Open Date 08/06/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Division Chief - Division of Hospital Medicine Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006045 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 03/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Division of Hospital Medicine within the Department of Medicine at the University of North Carolina School of Medicine seeks an accomplished academic physician to serve as its next Division Chief. This is an Open Rank faculty position that includes an at-will secondary appointment as Division Chief. The appointment will be at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor commensurate with experience and accomplishments. UNC Hospital Medicine is a nationally recognized academic division within a top-ranked academic health system, providing care across multiple sites, including UNC Medical Center in Chapel Hill and UNC Hospitals Hillsborough. The Division Chief will lead a large and dynamic group of academic hospitalists and play a critical role in advancing the division’s missions of clinical excellence, medical education, research, quality improvement, patient safety, and faculty development. The successful candidate will be a visionary, collaborative, and innovative leader with a demonstrated record of accomplishment in academic medicine. The Division Chief will provide strategic leadership for a robust academic practice and foster the continued growth of the division’s programs in research, education, complex clinical care, and quality and safety initiatives. Responsibilities will include a combination of administrative, clinical, educational, and scholarly activities, while partnering closely with departmental and health system leadership to support the division’s continued growth and success. The Division Chief will be expected to recruit, develop, mentor, and retain outstanding faculty and staff; promote an inclusive and collaborative culture; advance educational programs for learners at all levels; and support scholarly productivity across the division. The ideal candidate will possess exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, sound judgment, and the ability to effectively lead a multifaceted academic division through a period of continued growth and innovation. In addition to division leadership responsibilities, the selected candidate will maintain an active clinical practice within UNC Hospital Medicine, with opportunities to participate in both teaching and non-teaching services across UNC Health facilities. UNC Health offers a highly competitive compensation package, comprehensive benefits, and robust support for professional development. Located in Chapel Hill, North Carolina, the position provides the opportunity to live and work in one of the nation’s most desirable academic communities. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements M.D. or D.O. medical degree. Completion of residency training in Internal Medicine or Combined Internal Medicine-Pediatrics. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Board Certified in Internal Medicine. Demonstrated leadership experience in academic medicine, hospital medicine, healthcare administration, medical education, research, quality improvement, or related areas. Record of clinical excellence and commitment to patient-centered care. Evidence of scholarly achievement and academic productivity appropriate for faculty rank. Strong leadership, mentorship, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to inspire and develop faculty, foster collaboration, and effectively manage a complex academic division. Significant leadership experience within academic hospital medicine. Experience leading programs related to quality, safety, operations, education, research, faculty development, or healthcare innovation. Demonstrated success in strategic planning, recruitment, mentorship, and building high-performing teams. A clear vision for advancing the mission and impact of an academic division of hospital medicine. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Required Documents: Curriculum vitae, cover letter Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/323503 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Karen Clayton, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email karen_clayton@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327058": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Teaching Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Teaching Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will only be accepted online. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a teaching statement. Applicants are required to identify the names, titles, email addresses and phone numbers of three professional references when applying. Each reference provider will be contacted to upload their letter of support. Applications will be reviewed beginning November 2026. Questions should be directed to: Chair, Applied Physical Sciences Search Committee, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, NC 27599-3050; aps_tap_search@unc.edu. Posting Information Posting Information Department Applied Physical Sciences - 318100 Posting Open Date 10/13/2026 Application Deadline 01/04/2027 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Teaching Assistant Professor Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006166 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and/or Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! The Department of Applied Physical Sciences ( APS , which will be renamed to Applied Sciences and Engineering effective Fall 2027) at the University of North Carolina invites applications for a Teaching Assistant Professor ( TAP ). This position is a 3-year, 9-month, permanent, fixed-term faculty appointment. The individual in the position will be evaluated annually for teaching and service. APS has developed an innovative, general engineering undergraduate major with tracks in materials engineering and environmental engineering. The APS program capitalizes on the strengths of UNC in the liberal arts to train students to address the complex, interdisciplinary challenges of today. We seek a dynamic educator who will thrive in this innovative environment and is prepared to design, improve upon, and teach undergraduate courses using pedagogy informed by engineering education research. The successful candidate will join a cohesive and innovative group of faculty who are dedicated to teaching excellence. The TAP will teach three classes per semester including first year classes, engineering foundations courses, and upper-level electives. The TAP will also be expected to provide service to the department by working with the Director of Undergraduate Studies to support the implementation of the new undergraduate program. This could include the development of one or more of the following: an assessment plan, peer teaching oversight, faculty mentoring, and undergraduate laboratory activities. There could be opportunities to teach summer school classes. A PhD in Engineering, Materials Science, Applied Sciences, Engineering Education or a related field is required. Candidates with demonstrated experience in innovative and evidence-based teaching methods will be considered most competitive, including the following: prior teaching in engineering courses, especially materials engineering; industry-education relations; teaching which is responsive to developing artificial intelligence tools. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Applied Physical Sciences ( APS ) turns ideas into impact in three areas: health, energy, and water. It pursues those goals through innovations in materials discovery, design, and characterization; devices and instrumentation; and computation and artificial intelligence. Launched in 2013 as the first new science department in the College of Arts and Sciences in nearly 40 years, APS combines applied sciences and engineering to pursue team-based, interdisciplinary research in health, energy, and water. That same hands-on spirit powers BeAM (Be A Maker), APS’s university-wide making initiative, anchored by a 3,400-square-foot makerspace in Murray Hall that serves the entire Carolina community. Position Summary The Teaching Assistant Professor will teach three classes per semester including first year classes, engineering foundational courses, and upper-level electives in materials and engineering. The TAP will also be expected to provide service to the department by working with the Director of Undergraduate Studies to support the implementation of the new undergraduate program. This could include the development of one or more of the following: an assessment plan, student advising processes, peer teaching oversight, faculty mentoring, and undergraduate laboratory activities. This position may also have opportunities to teach summer school classes. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Candidate must hold a Ph.D (or equivalent degree) in Applied Sciences, Materials Science, or any Engineering discipline, including Engineering Education. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Candidates with demonstrated experience in innovative and evidence-based teaching methods will be considered most competitive. Prior teaching experience in engineering courses, especially materials engineering, is desirable. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Applications will only be accepted online. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a teaching statement. Applicants are required to identify the names, titles, email addresses and phone numbers of three professional references when applying. Each reference provider will be contacted to upload their letter of support. Applications will be reviewed beginning November 2026. Questions should be directed to: Chair, Applied Physical Sciences Search Committee, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, NC 27599-3050; aps_tap_search@unc.edu. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326763 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Richard Goldberg, Teaching Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email rgoldber@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree/degree level? Masters PharmaD DNP PhD JD MLS/MIS DVM DDS MD Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327057": {
      "title": "Community Navigator",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Community Navigator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Community Navigator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Psychiatry - YBH Butner - 412217 Posting Open Date 09/18/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Community Navigator Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006101 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 11/09/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Community Navigator will work with the treatment teams at the Youth Behavioral Hospital to provide short term care coordination and connection to resources and support for individuals and their guardians who are transitioning from inpatient to outpatient care. As the position grows the Community Navigator will serve as a resource for individuals and families navigating the health care system. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Candidates must have must have a Master’s degree in Social Work or a relevant human services field. The following licenses will be considered: LCSW , LCMHC , LCSW -A. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Excellent communication skills, proven rapport-building, and knowledge of existing community resources is preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325584 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Morgan Elliston, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email moellist@ad.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327038": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Adjunct Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department SOE Academic - 340200 Application Deadline 04/15/2027 Position Type Visiting / Part-time Faculty Working Title Adjunct Faculty Appointment Type Adjunct Faculty Position Number 20052237, 20046048, 80785323, 80782881, 20069903, 20070767, 20076904, 80752757, 20047277, 80781497, 20060345, 80780411, 80755572, 80501563, 80767482, 80781565, 80785367, 80785369, 80779688 Vacancy ID F003695 Full-time/Part-time Part-Time Temporary Hours per week 0.01 FTE 0 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date Estimated duration of appointment One year Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks that include numerous retail and restaurant discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates for performing arts events. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The School of Education is an academic unit reporting to the Provost. The School is a major center of research, teaching, and public service within the State of North Carolina, the nation, and the world. The School offers a full range of undergraduate and graduate programs. The mission of the School of Education is to conduct research, and generate basic and applied knowledge about human development, educational technology and entrepreneurship, teaching and learning, school counseling, school psychology, administration, as well as educational policy and leadership; prepare leaders in the profession of education by conducting outstanding research, teaching, and service; and assist in the development of strong and effective public schools in North Carolina. In order to fulfill its mission, the School is organized into three academic divisions: (1) Culture, Curriculum, & Teacher Education ( CCATE ), (2) Learning, Development & Psychological Sciences ( LDPS ), and (3) Educational Policy, Organization, & Leadership ( EPOL ). Position Summary The School of Education hires part-time non-salaried faculty to supervise and/or teach masters and doctoral students who will be future school personnel (e.g. School Principals, Counselors, Superintendents, etc.). Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Advanced knowledge and experience in the subject matter. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Prefer a master or doctorate degree in Education or related field (e.g. School Leadership, School Counseling, School Psychology, etc.). Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/327036 Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Catherine Vorick, HR Director Department Contact Telephone or Email cvorick@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Academic Personnel Office at facultyrecruitment@unc.edu . Please note: The Academic Personnel Office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
