    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326942": {
      "title": "Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Virtual Intensive Outpatient Program",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Virtual Intensive Outpatient Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Virtual Intensive Outpatient Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates may apply by going to https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326741 and attaching a curriculum vitae and letter of application. Please include the names of 2-3 references. Posting Information Posting Information Department Psychiatry - General - 412202 Posting Open Date 10/13/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Virtual Intensive Outpatient Program Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006158 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 01/11/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary Flexible work arrangements, including virtual/hybrid work locations, are an integral part of the School of Medicine’s Working Forward initiative. As such, this position’s work location is designated as virtual. Please note that the designated work location is subject to change based on the unit’s business needs. The Department of Psychiatry is seeking a full-time fixed-term faculty member at the rank of Clinical Instructor to work in the Virtual Intensive Outpatient Program. Treatment services include clinical assessments, individual/family therapy and group therapy to patients who are being referred after a psychiatric hospitalization and still needing more intensive services than traditional therapy or patients being referred by community providers to avoid psychiatric hospitalization. The clinician will provide short-term therapeutic services and case management services as part of the treatment team. Duties will include completing comprehensive clinical assessments, as needed, developing treatment plans, facilitating groups and individual sessions, collaborating with patients, family members, and others involved in patient’s care, and educating patients and family members on available resources. Document all clinical work thoroughly in the EMR within established time frames. Participate in team meetings and other departmental meetings and trainings. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Applicants must have a Master’s degree in Clinical Social Work, Counseling or a relevant field and have a full North Carolina licensure to practice ( LCSW or LCMHC ). Provisional licensees are not eligible. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Experience working with adolescents and young adults preferred. Experience facilitating group therapy is preferred but not required. Experience providing leadership and psychiatric services as part of a team is also preferred. Additionally, it is desired that the successful candidate will have strong clinical and diagnostic skills. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Interested candidates may apply by going to https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326741 and attaching a curriculum vitae and letter of application. Please include the names of 2-3 references. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326741 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Carla Feuerstein, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email carla_feuerstein@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity office at (919) 966-3576 or send an email to equalopportunity@unc.edu. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326936": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Emergency Medicine - 411201 Posting Open Date 05/19/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005934 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 11/02/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary This position will be part of an embedded emergency department-palliative care team comprised of dual-trained emergency medicine and palliative care physicians. Physicians will work 0.50 FTE traditional emergency department shifts and 0.50 FTE dedicated palliative care consults in the emergency department. Emergency department shifts will be conducted in both the Chapel Hill campus and Hillsborough campus emergency departments, treating both adult and pediatric patients. Embedded palliative care shifts will be at the Chapel Hill campus. Physicians are required to assess and attend to patients who enter the hospital’s emergency room. They immediately treat any injuries, infections, or other conditions to stabilize patients. Emergency department doctors request medical tests for patients, create treatment plans, and recommend patients to appropriate specialists. When providing palliative care consultation in the department, physicians will work closely with the emergency department team and broader palliative care/hospice team to care for seriously ill patients. Physicians will support medical decision-making, symptom management, and psychosocial needs for patients and families in the emergency department. This is a full-time position at 1.0 FTE . Clinical Instructors, Clinical Assistants, Clinical Associates, and Clinical Professors will be considered. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD, DO, or equivalent. Must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in both emergency medicine and hospice and palliative medicine. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Emergency Medicine/Palliative Care Fellowship Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319083 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Kelly Armstrong Department Contact Telephone or Email kelly_armstrong@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326929": {
      "title": "Post-Doc Research Associate",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Research Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Lampe Biomedical Engineering - 424601 Posting Open Date 10/13/2026 Application Deadline 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Research Associate Vacancy ID PDS004999 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent upon NIH Scale Proposed Start Date 10/13/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our research team is uniquely positioned in the Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering bridging UNC Chapel Hill and NC State University, and actively collaborate with clinicians, pharmacists, and industry in basic science, preclinical, and translational research. UNC Chapel Hill is an exciting place to perform biomedical ultrasound research. The ‘triangle’ formed between UNC , Duke, and NCSU has one of the greatest concentrations of ultrasound research labs in the country, and provides outstanding opportunities for broad collaborations. Our ULTRASONC Consortium is a team of more than 20 faculty working on the development of new ultrasound technologies, and provides an immense base of expertise, equipment, and training opportunities. The resources of the UNC Biomedical Research Imaging Center, the UNC School of Pharmacy, the Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer Center, and the NCSU College of Veterinary Medicine provide powerful opportunities for research teams to develop translational projects. Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary A Postdoctoral position is currently open in the Dayton Lab within the Lampe Joint Biomedical Engineering Dept. This research position will lead research in advanced ultrasound imaging and ultrasound therapeutics. Post-docs with background in therapeutic delivery or imaging physics/engineering will both be considered for different projects. Our research group has more than 3000 sq feet of research space equipped with state of the art equipment for biomedical acoustics, including 1024 channel Verasonics engines, multiple clinical ultrasound systems, HIFU systems, and high speed cameras, as well as facilities for contrast agent and drug delivery vehicle pharmacoengineering. Current research areas include super-resolution imaging, neuromodulation, molecular imaging, superharmonic imaging, sonothrombolysis, BBB opening, targeted drug delivery, acoustically mediated immunotherapy, and bioeffects studies. Candidates will both conduct independent work and work with a team to conduct bench and translational research, analyze data, prepare papers, reports, and contribute to proposals. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in biomedical engineering, electrical engineering, physics, chemistry, or a related field for imaging physics or acoustic therapeutics. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Excellent writing and communication skills are required. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Previous Research and Laboratory experience Special Physical/Mental Requirements Must be able to lift at least 25 pounds for movement of equipment. Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326913 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Samantha Caudill - HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email scaudil@email.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this position? Association of Fundraising Professionals Triangle Chapter of Association of Fundraising Professionals Higher Ed Jobs Diversity in Higher Education Council for Advancement and Support of Education Inside Higher Ed SOG/MPA listserv UNC-CH Development listserv UNC-CH website Other What is your highest degree and what field is it in? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326911": {
      "title": "Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatrist - Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatrist - Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Child & Adolescent Psychiatrist - Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates may apply by going to https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247375 and attaching a curriculum vitae and letter of application. Please include the names of 2-3 reference writers. Posting Information Posting Information Department Psychiatry - General - 412202 Posting Open Date 01/05/2023 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Child & Adolescent Psychiatrist - Open Rank Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0004389 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 09/03/2023 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC School of Medicine has a rich tradition of excellence and care. Our mission is to improve the health and wellbeing of North Carolinians, and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. We strive to promote faculty, staff, and learner development in a diverse, respectful environment where our colleagues demonstrate professionalism, enhance learning, and create personal and professional sustainability. We optimize our partnership with the UNC Health System through close collaboration and commitment to service. OUR VISION Our vision is to be the nation’s leading public school of medicine. We are ranked 2nd in primary care education among all US schools of medicine and 5th among public peers in NIH research funding. Our Allied Health Department is home to five top-ranked divisions, and we are home to 18 top-ranked clinical and basic science departments in NIH research funding. OUR MISSION Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. Patient Care: We will promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We will prepare tomorrow’s health care professionals and biomedical researchers by facilitating learning within innovative curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education. We will cultivate outstanding teaching and research faculty, and we will recruit outstanding students and trainees from highly diverse backgrounds to create a socially responsible, highly skilled workforce. Research: We will develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers, and resources. We will provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our University to support outstanding research. We will foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic, and population research. Position Summary The UNC Department of Child & Adolescent Psychiatry is seeking a psychiatrist to provide inpatient clinical services to children and young adults in the Child & Adolescent inpatient and outpatient programs. This is a full-time fixed term (clinical) position The rank will be based on the qualifications of the applicants. We anticipate hiring a child and adolescent psychiatrist to work in the adolescent inpatient setting and an adult or child adolescent psychiatrist on the young adult unit at the new Child & Adolescent Psychiatry facility in Butner, NC. The position will be at least 50% inpatient and opportunity for up to 100% inpatient. The position can include outpatient work including in-person and/or virtual care services. Duties also include teaching/supervising fellows, residents, medical students and other trainees from a variety of disciplines. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Applicants must have an MD or DO, be BC/BE, and be eligible for North Carolina licensure. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience The successful candidate should have strong clinical skills and demonstrated teaching skills necessary to enable them to successfully provide educational and training experiences for medical students, residents, fellows, other health care trainees, and clinicians. Candidates should have clinical experience working with children, adolescents, and young adults. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Interested candidates may apply by going to https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247375 and attaching a curriculum vitae and letter of application. Please include the names of 2-3 reference writers. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/247375 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Morgan Elliston, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email moellist@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326908": {
      "title": "Open Rank - MFM/Critical Care Specialist",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank - MFM/Critical Care Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank - MFM/Critical Care Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department OBGYN-MFM - 412440 Posting Open Date 06/04/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank - MFM/Critical Care Specialist Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005980 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Commensurate with experience Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The University of North Carolina’s Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is recruiting a tenure track or variable track Maternal-Fetal Medicine Specialist with expertise in critical care obstetrics to provide inpatient and outpatient care to high-risk obstetric patients, including those requiring intensive care management. This is a unique opportunity to serve as the clinical and academic leader of Critical Care MFM at UNC , with responsibilities extending well beyond direct ICU service. The successful candidate will be expected to: (1) provide consultative and co-management critical care services for pregnant and postpartum patients; (2) lead the development and implementation of evidence-based critical care protocols for obstetric patients; (3) build and direct a joint MFM -Critical Care fellowship program in collaboration with relevant departments; and (4) develop and expand tele-critical care (e- ICU ) capacity to extend critical care expertise to obstetric patients across UNC Health’s regional network. Additional responsibilities include education of medical students, residents, and fellows, and active participation in the division’s research mission. The division’s clinical programs include high-risk obstetric care, perinatal consultation, prenatal diagnosis, ultrasound, genetic services, invasive fetal therapy, and perinatal outreach. Division faculty members are engaged participants in the activities of UNC’s Collaborative for Maternal and Infant Health (www.mombaby.org), which provides multidisciplinary care coordination for families referred for fetal malformations. Division members actively participate in student and resident teaching and provide subspecialty training for six Maternal Fetal Medicine fellows through its 3-year American Board of Obstetrics & Genecology ( ABOG ) approved fellowship program. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or DO degree, completed a 4-year ACGME approved OB- GYN residency and completed a 3-year ACGME or ABOG approved fellowship in Maternal-Fetal Medicine. Must be Board Eligible or Board Certified in both Obstetrics and Gynecology and Maternal-Fetal Medicine. Board Certified/Board Eligible/Active Candidate in both OB- GYN and Maternal-Fetal Medicine. Fellowship training or equivalent clinical experience in critical care medicine is strongly preferred. Demonstrated competence in maternal medicine, prenatal diagnosis, and the management of critically ill obstetric patients. Commitment to excellence in medical education, quality improvement, and health equity. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Interest in program development, protocol leadership, or tele-medicine initiatives is highly desirable. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/320243 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Laura Bartholomew, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email llbarth@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326907": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Radiology- Emergency Radiology - 412814 Posting Open Date 05/26/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005951 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 11/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary Flexible work arrangements, including virtual and hybrid work locations, are an integral part of the School of Medicine’s Working Forward initiative. This position may be eligible for a virtual or hybrid work arrangement, in accordance with UNC policy and subject to approval based on the unit’s business needs. Please note that the approved work location may change over time to meet operational requirements. Position Description The Department of Radiology at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking an Emergency Radiologist to join the Division of Emergency Radiology. This position supports the department’s clinical, educational, and academic missions within a high-volume academic medical center and Level I Trauma Center environment. The Division of Emergency Radiology provides high-quality imaging interpretation services for emergency department patients at UNC Medical Center and affiliated clinical partners. Emergency radiologists work closely with Emergency Medicine, Acute Care Surgery (Trauma Surgery), and multidisciplinary clinical teams to support the rapid diagnosis and management of complex trauma, surgical emergencies, and urgent medical conditions. Division faculty are highly skilled in the interpretation of radiography (x-ray), fluoroscopy, ultrasound, computed tomography (CT), and magnetic resonance imaging ( MRI ) performed in the emergency setting. Faculty provide timely and accurate diagnostic interpretations that directly support acute patient care and emergent clinical decision-making. This position follows a 7 days on / 14 days off schedule structure. Evening and overnight shift opportunities may be available, with scheduling details evolving alongside continued division growth. Position Responsibilities Interpret emergency and trauma imaging studies, including radiography, fluoroscopy, ultrasound, CT, and MRI examinations performed in the acute care setting Provide timely, high-quality diagnostic interpretations to support emergency department and trauma patient care Collaborate closely with Emergency Medicine, Acute Care Surgery, and multidisciplinary clinical teams in the management of emergent conditions Participate in the education and supervision of diagnostic radiology residents, fellows, and medical students Participate in departmental, divisional, and institutional quality improvement initiatives Engage in scholarly, academic, or research activities consistent with departmental needs No expectation to interpret MRI or pediatric imaging studies, and no requirement to perform procedures as part of the Emergency Radiology Division clinical practice. Appointment Details This is an open rank, fixed term faculty appointment at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Board certified or board eligible Radiologist Fellowship training in any radiology subspecialty (including, but not limited to, Abdominal Imaging, Cardiothoracic Imaging, Musculoskeletal Imaging, or Neuroradiology) or equivalent clinical experience Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary clinical teams Interest or experience in resident and fellow education in an academic medical setting Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319610 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Alexis Evans, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email alexis_evans@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326905": {
      "title": "Pediatric Otolaryngology Faculty (Open Rank)",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Pediatric Otolaryngology Faculty (Open Rank) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Pediatric Otolaryngology Faculty (Open Rank) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Otolaryngology (Ent) - 414401 Posting Open Date 10/13/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Pediatric Otolaryngology Faculty (Open Rank) Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006165 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 12/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Otolaryngology/Head & Neck Surgery at University of North Carolina – Chapel Hill seeks a new member to join its Division of Pediatric Otolaryngology/Head and Neck Surgery as a fixed-term track faculty member; this is a fixed-term open rank recruitment; academic rank will be awarded at the level commensurate with experience. This role offers the opportunity to provide comprehensive, family centered care for infants, children, and adolescents with a wide spectrum of routine and complex ear, nose, throat, and head and neck conditions for children and families across North Carolina and the Southeastern United States. The Department’s faculty members are a part of a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment, working closely with pediatric subspecialists, anesthesiology, speech language pathology, audiology, and other allied health partners. The position includes active involvement in teaching and mentoring medical students, residents, and fellows, as well as opportunities to contribute to UNC’s academic mission through research, clinical trials, and ongoing scholarly activity. UNC offers robust clinical resources, a strong referral base, and a supportive academic culture that values innovation, collaboration, and professional growth. The successful candidate should have expertise in all aspects of Pediatric Otolaryngology/Head and Neck Surgery and an interest in contributing to a very strong clinical and research program in Pediatric Otolaryngology/Head and Neck Surgery. Special expertise and an interest in sub-specialization including Pediatric Airway/Aerodigestive Surgery, Pediatric Otology including Pediatric Hearing Loss and Cochlear Implantation, Craniofacial Surgery, Pediatric Head and Neck Surgery, Rhinology and Endoscopic Skull Base Surgery, and Research in Pediatric Otolaryngology/Head and Neck Surgery and have demonstrated the potential for teaching, patient care and clinical research are encouraged to apply for this position. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements M.D., D.O., or equivalent. Board eligible or board certified in Otolaryngology/Head & Neck Surgery. Fellowship trained in Pediatric Otolaryngology/Head and Neck Surgery. Must be licensed or eligible for licensure to practice medicine within the state of North Carolina. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a dedication to patient care and education. Background in teaching and mentoring within an academic or clinical setting. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326858 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Emily Boimare, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email emily_boimare@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other * Do you have experience working with adults and pediatric patients in a clinical care setting? Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
