    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326418": {
      "title": "General Surgeon",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | General Surgeon Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina General Surgeon Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Surgery - Acute Care Trauma - 414040 Posting Open Date 10/02/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title General Surgeon Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006140 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 01/25/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Surgery at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking applications for a full-time academic General Surgeon to join the existing group of five UNC faculty based surgeons who have a focused practice of General Surgery within the community. The practice has some subspecialty focus as well given the fellowship training of the current group. This position will include clinical practice at both UNC Health Care Hillsborough Hospital and the UNC Chatham Hospital. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive general surgery services at both campuses while supporting the Department’s mission to expand access to high-quality surgical care throughout central North Carolina and building an elective practice focused on community general surgery. UNC Health Care Hillsborough is a 163-bed community hospital that combines the culture and accessibility of a community hospital with the advanced technology and expertise of UNC Medical Center. It has 10 ORs including 2 with Robotic surgery capability. The campus includes an outpatient medical office building with clinic and procedure space, as well as a busy emergency department. The Chatham hospital is a 25 bed facility with 2 ORs, an outpatient medical office building, and an emergency room. The Department of Surgery is committed to growing both elective and emergency surgical services at Hillsborough and Chatham while extending specialty surgical care closer to the communities we serve. Clinical responsibilities will include elective and urgent general surgery, emergency general surgery call coverage at the Hillsborough campus, outpatient consultation and follow-up at both campuses, and collaboration with multidisciplinary teams across the UNC Health system. The successful candidate will work closely with colleagues across the Department of Surgery to ensure seamless coordination of care across campuses. This position is being recruited as an Open Rank, Open Track appointment at an FTE between 0.5 and 1.0, with academic rank commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. The faculty member will be expected to perform clinical duties while fulfilling the academic responsibilities of an educational institution. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the Department’s three core missions of clinical care, education, and research. Individuals who demonstrate exceptional skills and achievements may be considered for leadership opportunities within the Department of Surgery. Leadership roles are not guaranteed and will be dependent upon the needs of the Department of Surgery and UNC Health. Faculty members are expected to participate in the education of medical students, residents, and other learners through clinical teaching and mentorship in both the academic medical center and community hospital settings. Candidates with interests in clinical research, outcomes research, quality improvement, health services research, surgical education, global surgery, or other scholarly endeavors are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to providing exceptional, patient-centered surgical care while advancing access to high-quality surgical services in a community practice environment. Candidates should possess expertise in a broad range of general surgical procedures, including minimally invasive surgery. The selected candidate must be collaborative, team-oriented, and able to work effectively with colleagues across multiple surgical specialties, hospital campuses, and interdisciplinary care teams. Individuals who exhibit exceptional skills and achievements may be considered for a leadership position within the department of surgery. Leadership roles are not guaranteed and are dependent upon the current needs of our surgical programs. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree. Board Certified or Board Eligible in General Surgery. Eligible for medical licensure in the State of North Carolina. Eligible for hospital privileges at UNC Health facilities. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Interest in expanding access to surgical care within community populations. Experience with elective and emergency general surgery. Interest or experience in minimally invasive and robotic surgical techniques. Commitment to excellence in clinical care, medical education, and academic scholarship, Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively in multidisciplinary teams. Demonstrated commitment to patient-centered care, quality improvement, and continuous professional development. Interest in clinical research, outcomes research, surgical education, or quality improvement initiatives is desirable. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326280 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Elizabeth Hubbard, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email elizabeth_hubbard@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326417": {
      "title": "Open Rank Fixed-Term Faculty Interventional Pulmonary",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Fixed-Term Faculty Interventional Pulmonary Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Fixed-Term Faculty Interventional Pulmonary Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Med-Pulmonary - 411480 Posting Open Date 09/09/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Fixed-Term Faculty Interventional Pulmonary Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006081 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Division of Pulmonary Diseases and Critical Care Medicine at the UNC School of Medicine is recruiting for a full-time faculty member with expertise in Interventional Pulmonary Medicine. Duties include, but are not limited to, seeing referrals for diagnostic and therapeutic procedures related to known or suspected lung cancer, thoracic metastasis, infectious or interstitial diseases of the lung, and pleural diseases. They will be responsible for management of benign and malignant obstructive airway lesions, lung malignancies requiring endoluminal therapies, robotic assisted evaluation of suspicious parenchymal lung lesions, acute and chronic pleural processes, and performance of bedside tracheostomy placement. These duties will be conducted in the inpatient and ambulatory care settings. They will be responsible for teaching pulmonary procedures to fellow trainees in Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine and subspecialty fellows in Interventional Pulmonary. They will also have opportunities to attend in the Medical Intensive Care Unit with additional related teaching duties. Additionally, the position will include opportunities to conduct clinical research related to cancer diagnostics/therapeutics, pleural diseases, and innovative interventional procedures. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Applicants must hold an MD or DO degree and be BC/BE in Internal Medicine, Pulmonary Diseases, Critical Care Medicine, and Interventional Pulmonology. Candidates will have completed a minimum of one year of interventional pulmonary fellowship training. Candidates should have experience performing advanced diagnostic and rigid bronchoscopy, robotic assisted navigational bronchoscopy, bedside tracheostomy, thoracic ultrasound, thoracentesis, chest tube placement, tunneled pleural catheter placement, medical thoracoscopy and management of complex pleural processes. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Formal training in clinical research methods or experience in formal GME education is preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324993 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Rhonda Nord Department Contact Telephone or Email rhonda_nord@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Are you board certified/board eligible in Internal Medicine, Pulmonary Diseases, Critical Care Medicine, and Interventional Pulmonology? Yes No Have you completed a minimum of one year of interventional pulmonary fellowship training? Yes No Do you have experience performing advanced diagnostic and rigid bronchoscopy, robotic assisted navigational bronchoscopy, bedside tracheostomy, thoracic ultrasound, thoracentesis, chest tube placement, tunneled pleural catheter placement, medical thoracoscopy and management of complex pleural processes? Yes No Do you have the preferred formal training in clinical research methods or experience in formal GME education? Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326416": {
      "title": "System Executive Director - Advanced Heart Failure &amp; Transplant Network",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | System Executive Director - Advanced Heart Failure &amp; Transplant Network Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina System Executive Director - Advanced Heart Failure & Transplant Network Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Medicine - Cardiology - 411405 Posting Open Date 10/02/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title System Executive Director - Advanced Heart Failure & Transplant Network Appointment Type Admin Appointment with Faculty Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006141 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience/Qualifications Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Division of Cardiology in the Department of Medicine seeks an accomplished physician leader in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology to serve as System Executive Director of the Advanced Heart Failure & Transplant Network for UNC Health. This position will provide strategic leadership for the continued growth, integration, and advancement of a comprehensive statewide network for advanced heart failure, mechanical circulatory support, cardiogenic shock, and heart transplantation. Working collaboratively with physicians, administrators, surgeons, researchers, and clinical teams across UNC Health, the Executive Director will lead efforts to develop and implement a shared vision for network growth, clinical excellence, quality improvement, innovation, and patient access. The individual will be responsible for fostering alignment across academic and community-based programs, strengthening referral pathways, expanding access to advanced heart failure therapies, and advancing the system’s mission in patient care, research, and education. This recruitment is for an Open Rank faculty position within the Division of Cardiology, with rank to be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications, experience, and accomplishments. The successful candidate will hold a primary faculty appointment in the Department of Medicine and a secondary administrative leadership appointment as System Executive Director of the Advanced Heart Failure & Transplant Network, which includes an associated administrative supplement. Clinical responsibilities will include the care of patients with advanced heart failure, heart transplantation, mechanical circulatory support, and cardiogenic shock, while supporting the academic missions of research, education, and service. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD required. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience * Board Certified in Cardiovascular Disease * Advanced training and expertise in Advanced Heart Failure and Transplant Cardiology * Demonstrated leadership experience within a major Advanced Heart Failure, LVAD , and/or Heart Transplant program * Experience working across multidisciplinary clinical teams * Strong interest in system development, physician engagement, and network growth * Academic accomplishments consistent with appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor level preferred * Proven track record in clinical research and program development preferred Special Physical/Mental Requirements . Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326300 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Briana Marini, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email briana_marini@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326373": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Critical Game Studies",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Critical Game Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Assistant Professor of Critical Game Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit the following documents: A cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, a twenty- to twenty-five page writing sample, and a syllabus for a course focused on critical game studies. If applicable, you can also submit a sample of material related to critical making. In addition, please submit the names of four references as part of your application. Letters of recommendation will be requested later and required for candidates to proceed to the interview stage. Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026. Please upload all necessary documents to the application portal. If you have any search-related questions, feel free to contact the Search Committee Chair Martin Johnson at mlj@email.unc.edu. For any technical issues or application portal-related issues, don’t hesitate to get in touch with Sujata Paudel at paudels@unc.edu. Posting Information Posting Information Department English and Comp Literature - 311500 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Assistant Professor of Critical Game Studies Appointment Type Tenured/Tenure Track Vacancy ID FAC0006139 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Commensurate with education/experience Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! The Department of English and Comparative Literature in the College of Arts & Sciences at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is looking for an applicant who engages with Critical Game Studies methods and scholarship in their teaching and research. Candidates should utilize interdisciplinary humanities approaches for analyzing, participating, and creating in games studies. We welcome approaches that engage in games studies’ major intellectual strands, such as game narratives and narrative critique, game aesthetics, ludology, critical making, design, technology studies, or the rhetoric of games and gaming. We seek candidates who are confident in producing cross-disciplinary, collaborative, and experimental games research. A record of research and publication will show the ability to translate hands-on work into theoretically informed and peer-recognized scholarship. Facility with interdisciplinary work will be evident through expertise in multiple areas of study and the creative combination of approaches. Our department offers a wide variety of courses in game studies, and we are looking for candidates who are well prepared to teach in our current curriculum, as well as contribute to its ongoing development in this emerging field. Candidates will also mentor undergraduate and graduate students in critical game studies and, if relevant, their secondary fields of expertise. Strong evidence of leadership and participation in game studies programs and initiatives will show a collaborative model for academic work. Public outreach, the sharing of resources, and community building will demonstrate generosity and engagement. Candidates who apply for this position should demonstrate the traits described above and have a significant investment in critical game studies. They will work regularly with hands-on games studies methods, have a strong record of collaboration and working across disciplinary areas, and read and produce critical game studies scholarship. They may also have expertise in a complementary area of interest that would find a home in a department of English and comparative literature. Our department strengths include literary studies; film and media; rhetoric and composition; creative writing; digital humanities; Latina/o studies; and health humanities. We also seek to grow in areas of environmental humanities; disability studies; and new media studies. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of English and Comparative Literature is committed to hiring an exceptional teacher/scholar who brings energy and a fresh perspective to their research, pedagogy, and service and who is ready to teach in our Critical Game Studies program. We seek candidates who can contribute to UNC’s academic mission as a public institution, especially through commitment to diversity of perspective, intercultural understanding, and engagement with local resources and communities. We encourage candidates to consult our website to learn about the Department’s curriculum, values, and mission. Candidates working across disciplines are encouraged to apply. The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is the flagship institution of a strong state university system comprising 17 campuses across North Carolina; neighbor institutions within 25 miles include Duke University, North Carolina Central University, North Carolina State University, and Meredith College. Chapel Hill is a vibrant college town near the Research Triangle economic hub and 20 minutes from Raleigh-Durham International Airport. Position Summary The Department of English and Comparative Literature at the University of North Carolina at Chapel is recruiting an Assistant Professor of Critical Game Studies. The successful candidate’s duties will include teaching, research, and service. The position will teach a 2-2 load made up of graduate and undergraduate courses; contribute to both undergraduate and graduate curricula; mentor students; participate in select administrative activities; and engage in ongoing scholarly research. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Ph.D. English or a relevant field and instructional experience at the college level by the time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Demonstrated excellence in college-level teaching, a strong research portfolio, expertise in research methods, a history of collaboration, experience working in, or with, game studies programs, and evidence of administrative and service experience. Special Physical/Mental Requirements N/A Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions To apply, please submit the following documents: A cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, a twenty- to twenty-five page writing sample, and a syllabus for a course focused on critical game studies. If applicable, you can also submit a sample of material related to critical making. In addition, please submit the names of four references as part of your application. Letters of recommendation will be requested later and required for candidates to proceed to the interview stage. Review of applications will begin on October 19, 2026 and continue until November 30, 2026. Please upload all necessary documents to the application portal. If you have any search-related questions, feel free to contact the Search Committee Chair Martin Johnson at mlj@email.unc.edu. For any technical issues or application portal-related issues, don’t hesitate to get in touch with Sujata Paudel at paudels@unc.edu. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326110 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Martin Louis Johnson/Professor, Associate Department Chair Department Contact Telephone or Email mlj@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Writing/research Sample Sample Syllabus Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326371": {
      "title": "Post-Doc Research Associate",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Post-Doc Research Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Post-Doc Research Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Applied Physical Sciences - 318100 Posting Open Date 09/18/2026 Application Deadline 10/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Post-Doc Research Associate Vacancy ID PDS004970 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and/or Qualifications Proposed Start Date 11/02/2026 Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Launched in 2013, the Department of Applied Physical Sciences ( APS ) is the first new science department in the College of Arts and Sciences in nearly 40 years. APS lives in the collaborative space between science and engineering, combining knowledge and discovery with an engineering mindset, team-based science, and entrepreneurship to address real-world problems. Organized around ‘Ideas to Impacts,’ the department unites with campus themes in health, water and energy to help Carolina continue to be a leader in science innovation and the application of knowledge. APS has united numerous scientific entities on campus to further its mission of finding interdisciplinary solutions to real-world problems. Its newest endeavor, BeAM (Be A Maker), is a university-wide initiative that incorporates Making into research, education, and entrepreneurship. BeAM is comprised of several spaces, including a makerspace in Hanes Art Center, Carmichael Residence Hall, and a 3,400 square foot Makerspace in Murray Hall, all of which serve the entire UNC community. Position Summary This Postdoctoral Research Associate will develop novel optical, electrochemical, colorimetric, lateral flow and wearable sensors for various pathogens and analytes. The Research Associate should have an interest and research experience in biosensor development and performance using various receptors spanning proteins and antibodies, aptamers, nanoparticles, polymers, and small molecules from a variety of samples including sputum and cerebrospinal fluid ( CSF ) samples. Previous experience with cell biology and intracellular sensing, microfluidics, or 3D printing is a plus. In addition to bench research, the post-doctoral fellow will be actively involved with data analysis, writing scientific papers and grant proposals and presenting data at scientific meetings. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in Biotechnology, Biological Sciences or similar. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Experience with synthesis and characterization of nanomaterials, biomaterials, polymers, hydrogels, and wearable and implantable biosensors. Experienced in applying these materials to three-dimensional (3D) cell culture models and translational diagnostics or similar. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Skilled in the design, fabrication, and characterization of microfluidic systems, including continuous monitoring platforms, as well as advanced cell culture techniques and molecular and cellular assays. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325606 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Ronit Freeman, Associate Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email ronifree@email.unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326369": {
      "title": "Open Rank Physiatrist",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Physiatrist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Physiatrist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualified applicants should submit an application online at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326342. The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and at least two references. Applicants are required to identify the names, titles, email addresses and phone numbers of two professional references when applying. Reference providers identified by the applicant will be contacted via email with instructions for uploading their letters of support. Posting Information Posting Information Department Physical Medicine Rehab - 413401 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Physiatrist Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006145 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Commensurate with Experience Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (PM&R) at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking a fixed-term open rank BC/BE physiatrist to join our expanding academic department. Rank will be based on qualifications and experience. This position will encompass a mix of skilled nursing facility rehabilitation care, hospital consultations and outpatient responsibilities that focus on general rehab in the Raleigh NC region. This position will work closely with Advanced Practice Providers (APPs), Rex SNF and Rehab staff and administration, and will serve as the Medical Director of the Raleigh Skilled Nursing and Rehab Facility. This position will be expected and given academic time to participate in educational, research, and administrative activities associated with their academic appointment and related area of expertise. Some on call responsibility and participation in quality improvement projects is required. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements The successful candidate will be board eligible/board certified in PM&R. MD, DO, or equivalent required. Must have a passion for skilled nursing facility rehabilitation and a NC medical license/willingness to obtain state license. This position is also open but NOT limited to fellowship trained cancer rehabilitation physiatrists with an interest in outpatient cancer rehab and skilled nursing facility rehabilitation and palliative care. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience The ideal candidate will have excellent interpersonal and communication skills, a record of interdisciplinary collaboration, and have the desire to be involved in enhancing quality of patient care. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Qualified applicants should submit an application online at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326342. The application should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae (CV), and at least two references. Applicants are required to identify the names, titles, email addresses and phone numbers of two professional references when applying. Reference providers identified by the applicant will be contacted via email with instructions for uploading their letters of support. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326342 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Allison Williams, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email allison_williams@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326367": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Trainee",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Postdoctoral Trainee Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Postdoctoral Trainee Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Posting Information Posting Details Department Epidemiology - 463501 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Postdoctoral Scholar Position Title Postdoctoral Trainee Vacancy ID PDS004988 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Temporary Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Work Location Chapel Hill, NC Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Qualifications Proposed Start Date Estimated Duration of Appointment 12 Months Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities and is among is the top ten research universities in the nation for federal research expenditures as well as for federally funded social and behavioral sciences research and development. Here at Carolina, our highly skilled postdocs play a vital role in our research enterprise and towards our overall commitment to research excellence. Across many disciplines, postdocs contribute to the intellectual vitality of the University. They provide innovative ideas and perspectives, foster a stimulating research environment and advance knowledge within their fields. Postdocs are crucial members of our scientific research workforce, contributors to our research outputs and an important reason why Carolina is one of the leading public research institutions in the country. UNC -Chapel Hill offers postdocs comprehensive medical and vision coverage , paid leave, and benefits and services that support professional development and a healthy work/life balance. Chapel Hill regularly ranks as one of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, a reputation guided by the diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Epidemiology is one of the eight departments located in the Gillings School of Global Public Health. The department’s primary focus is to the development and application of research methods to understand the patterns and causes of health and disease, and the application of that knowledge to improving the health of populations. We provide strong training in research methods and opportunities for the application of epidemiology to a wide range of health problems through our research. The achievements of our faculty, staff, students, and alumni have enabled us to become one of the leading academic departments of epidemiology in the world. At UNC -CH, Epidemiology is one of the largest and most complex departments on campus. For FY25, Epidemiology was 5th among all departments and centers across campus in research funding at UNC Chapel Hill. The department has 38 Tenured-Tenure Track / 8 Joint Tenure-Track Faculty, 16 Fixed Term / 4 Joint Fixed Term Faculty, 120 Adjuncts, 31 EHRA Non-Faculty, 18 Postdocs, 20SHRA, 29 Temps, and 234 Students (148 PhD, 74 MPH , AND 12 MSCR ) for whom Epidemiology pays 146 as RA/TA/Trainees/Fellows. Total departmental budget of $49 million (FY25). Position Summary A National Research Service Award ( NRSA ) postdoctoral research fellowship is available in the Genetic Epidemiology of Heart, Lung, and Blood Traits Program at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill. The position is funded by the National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute, NIH . The goals are to support the training, career development, and professional growth of the post-doctoral fellow by fostering skills and knowledge in Genetic Epidemiology of Heart, Lung, and Blood Traits ( GENHLB ). The post-doctoral fellow will participate with mentors, other faculty, and peers in the Genetic Epidemiology Program in authoring publications, making presentations at scientific and/or professional meetings, and developing grant support. Responsibilities of the post-doctoral fellow are to work towards enhancing their substantive and methodological skills in genetic epidemiology and related disciplines. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements A doctoral degree (PhD) in Epidemiology, Human Genetics, Biostatistics, Bioinformatics or related field or a MD, DDS , or DVM degree combined with training in human genetics or epidemiology at the PhD or Master’s levels (or equivalent) is/are required. Required Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Due to Federally-mandated funding restrictions, the post-doctoral trainee MUST be a US citizen or permanent resident. A curriculum vitae reflecting scientific productivity in epidemiology, human genetics, heart, lung, and/or blood phenotypes and/or biomedical sciences is required. Participation in this program requires a commitment of at least 40 hours per week on research and training, without supplemental compensation from the NRSA award. Trainees may be able to work a limited number of hours in addition to the 40-hour commitment, if explicitly approved by the Program Director based on its contribution to the fellow’s training and professional development. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience - Special Physical/Mental Requirements Special Instructions For information on UNC Postdoctoral Benefits and Services click here Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326361 Posting Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Christy Avery, Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email christy_avery@unc.edu Postdoctoral Affairs Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Office of Postdoctoral Affairs at (919) 962-9982 or send an email to opahr@unc.edu . Please note: The Office of Postdoctoral Affairs will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Optional and Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Degree Transcripts Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you meet one of the eligibility criteria’s stated below for a NRSA Trainee appointment? * US Citizenship * Permanent Resident with a valid Alien Registration Card (Form I-551) status at the time of appointment Yes No Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326365": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide an additional writing sample; two are required. Upload the additional writing sample under \"Other Document.\" Upload only a statement of teaching philosophy; no evaluations are required. Posting Information Posting Information Department Linguistics - 311800 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/02/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Assistant Professor Appointment Type Tenured/Tenure Track Vacancy ID FAC0006134 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and/or Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Linguistics is an undergraduate and graduate academic unit in the College of Arts and Sciences whose primary purpose is to make new discoveries concerning the nature and history of human languages and to communicate the results of the field through teaching, research, and service. The Department offers undergraduate and masters programs in linguistics, with emphasis on phonetics, phonology, morphology, syntax, semantics, language acquisition, sociolinguistics, computational linguistics, and historical linguistics, and a joint MA/PhD program in Hispanic Linguistics in conjunction with the Department of Romance Studies. Position Summary The Department of Linguistics is recruiting for a tenure-track Assistant Professor specializing in Syntax/Semantics and Language Documentation. The responsibilities of this position include maintaining an active research program, teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, advising undergraduate honors theses and MA theses, and contributing service to the department and/or university. This position carries our regular teaching load for faculty with an active research agenda: two courses per semester. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Candidates must have a PhD in Linguistics or a related field. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Research expertise in syntax, semantics, or the syntax/semantics interface, along with experience in language documentation and/or linguistic fieldwork sufficient to advise student thesis projects in documentation or fieldwork. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Please provide an additional writing sample; two are required. Upload the additional writing sample under “Other Document.” Upload only a statement of teaching philosophy; no evaluations are required. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326163 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Brian Hsu, Associate Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email hsub@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Other Document List of References Writing/research Sample Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree/degree level? Masters PharmaD DNP PhD JD MLS/MIS DVM DDS MD Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326360": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Teaching Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Teaching Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326210 and submit a Curriculum Vitae/Resume and Cover Letter. Applicants may also submit a statement concerning teaching philosophy/evaluations and a sample syllabus, however, these two items are optional. At the time of application candidates will be required to identify the names, titles, and email addresses of 2 professional references. Recommenders identified by the applicant will be contacted via email with instructions for uploading their letters of support. Posting Information Posting Information Department Peace War and Defense - 316200 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/17/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Teaching Assistant Professor Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006144 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience/Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Curriculum in Peace, War, and Defense offers a long-standing interdisciplinary undergraduate major focused on questions of peace, conflict, and human security. PWAD faculty include academics from a range of social science and humanities disciplines, as well as professors of the practice with extensive experience in public service, the military, and diplomacy. This combination of academic faculty and professors of the practice provides PWAD students with a unique academic experience. Position Summary The Teaching Assistant Professor, with a specialization in international relations, will be in the Curriculum in Peace, War, and Defense ( PWAD ). The position will teach 3 courses per semester (fall and spring) in support of the academic programs offered by the Curriculum in Peace, War, and Defense. Courses will include the introductory course in peace and security studies. The candidate will also teach other courses in the PWAD curriculum related to their area of expertise. There are no research expectations associated with this position. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in political science, international relations, or related field. Demonstrated record of successful teaching performance. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Expertise in the empirical study of peace science, conflict resolution, conflict management, or post-conflict governance, as well as teaching introductory courses in International Relations (or similar) is preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Applicants must apply online at https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326210 and submit a Curriculum Vitae/Resume and Cover Letter. Applicants may also submit a statement concerning teaching philosophy/evaluations and a sample syllabus, however, these two items are optional. At the time of application candidates will be required to identify the names, titles, and email addresses of 2 professional references. Recommenders identified by the applicant will be contacted via email with instructions for uploading their letters of support. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326210 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Kayla Fleetwood, Dept. Manager Department Contact Telephone or Email fleetwok@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Sample Syllabus Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326337": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Cello and Ensemble Studies",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Cello and Ensemble Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Assistant Professor of Cello and Ensemble Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants are asked to submit: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for four references. Letters of recommendation are not required at the time of application. The committee may solicit additional materials including letters of recommendation, performance samples (recordings, videos, and other media), a sample syllabus, and a teaching statement that addresses strategies candidates might use in a public university setting where students reflect the socioeconomic, racial, religious, and other diverse characteristics across the state of North Carolina. Application review will begin on November 15, 2026. This offer of appointment is also contingent on documentation of employment eligibility. Posting Information Posting Information Department Music - 310300 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Assistant Professor of Cello and Ensemble Studies Appointment Type Tenured/Tenure Track Vacancy ID FAC0006142 Full-time/Part-time Full Time Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and/or Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! The Department of Music at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Assistant Professor of Music in cello performance with expertise in individual studio teaching and creative performance, along with a related research area, including but not limited to performance practice and/or ensemble direction. The department’s faculty includes composers, conductors and ensemble directors, performers, scholars, and sound engineers engaged in manifold creative practices in a liberal arts context. We seek a creative, collaborative, and intellectually curious colleague with a record of accomplishment and a clear trajectory for future excellence to teach individual performance instruction as well as courses and/or ensembles within our Transformations in Music Studies curriculum (https://music.unc.edu/undergraduate/transformations-in-music-studies-at-carolina/). We welcome applications from candidates whose work aligns with our departmental mission as outlined on our website (https://music.unc.edu/about/). Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Music at UNC -Chapel Hill offers a BMus and BA in Music and an MA and Ph.D. in Musicology for undergraduate and graduate students. Our educational mission is to teach music majors and non-majors, to connect the study of music to the larger understanding of the world, and to guide graduate students as researchers and teachers. We serve the public by presenting performances and academic lectures by students, faculty, and guest artists and scholars. We offer over one hundred concerts and recitals each year, and our facilities include a state-of-the-art auditorium with recording (audio and video) capabilities as well as lighting and sound systems. Our 60 full-time and part-time faculty teach approximately 2500 students during the academic year and another 200 during summer school. Through our teaching, research, and creative activities, we share music’s multiplicity of forms and meanings, connecting the study of music to the larger understanding of societies, and affirming music’s importance as an expression of humanity. Position Summary This position’s teaching load will comprise a combination of studio lessons, courses, and/or ensembles that equates to a 2+2 load. The successful candidate will demonstrate a record of accomplishment in cello performance, classroom and/or ensemble instruction, and forward-thinking research areas that complement a department and campus of diverse interests. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Master’s degree in cello performance or related area. A record of accomplishment in cello performance and creative activity as well as evidence of teaching excellence. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preference will be given for candidates holding a DMA or PhD in cello performance, and who have at least two years of classroom teaching experience at a university level. We welcome applications from candidates whose work aligns with our departmental mission as outlined on our website (https://music.unc.edu/about/). Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Applicants are asked to submit: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information for four references. Letters of recommendation are not required at the time of application. The committee may solicit additional materials including letters of recommendation, performance samples (recordings, videos, and other media), a sample syllabus, and a teaching statement that addresses strategies candidates might use in a public university setting where students reflect the socioeconomic, racial, religious, and other diverse characteristics across the state of North Carolina. Application review will begin on November 15, 2026. This offer of appointment is also contingent on documentation of employment eligibility. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326204 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Evan Feldman - Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email evanfeldman@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326335": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor of Opera and Voice",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Teaching Assistant Professor of Opera and Voice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Teaching Assistant Professor of Opera and Voice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A cover letter, curriculum vitae, three links to recent recordings demonstrating the applicant's vocal and/or musical productions, with recordings preferably from the past five years, and the names and contact information for four references. The committee may solicit additional materials including letters of recommendation, sample teaching materials and/or evaluations, a sample syllabus, and a teaching statement that addresses pedagogical strategies candidates might use in a public university setting where students reflect the varied socioeconomic, racial, religious, and other demographics of the state. Application review will begin on November 9, 2026. Posting Information Posting Information Department Music - 310300 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/09/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Teaching Assistant Professor of Opera and Voice Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006143 Full-time/Part-time Full Time Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience and/or Qualifications Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! The Department of Music at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill invites applications for a Teaching Assistant Professor of Music with expertise in Opera and Voice. We seek a pedagogically innovative and collaborative colleague who will direct UNC Opera and teach studio voice within the context of a broad liberal arts curriculum. This position is particularly well suited to a singer-teacher and opera director who is passionate about working with singers in a performance program that is undergraduate-only and welcomes students with a wide range of musical backgrounds, interests, and levels of prior experience. UNC Opera typically performs a scenes program in the fall and a full production in the spring. This course emphasizes the musical and dramatic aspects of role preparation and staging, rather than high-concept productions. Candidates with experience teaching across musical genres and styles, including classical, musical theatre, and contemporary vocal repertoire, are especially encouraged to apply. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Music at UNC -Chapel Hill offers a BMus and BA in Music for undergraduate students and an MA and Ph.D. in Musicology for graduate students. Our educational mission is to teach music majors and non-majors, to connect the study of music to a broader understanding of the world, and to guide graduate students as researchers and teachers. We serve the public by presenting performances and academic lectures by students, faculty, and guest artists and scholars. We offer over one hundred concerts and recitals each year, and our facilities include a state-of-the-art auditorium with recording capabilities (audio and video) as well as lighting and sound systems. Our 60 full-time and part-time faculty teach approximately 2500 students during the academic year and another 200 during summer school. Through our teaching, research, and creative activities, we share music’s multiplicity of forms and meanings, connecting the study of music to a broader understanding of societies and affirming music’s importance as an expression of humanity. Position Summary This is a full-time, teaching-track (non-tenure-track) position with an initial three-year appointment, eligible for renewal and promotion. The teaching assignment will be the equivalent of a 3+3 load, with specific responsibilities distributed among opera direction, private voice instruction, and classroom teaching. The precise distribution of responsibilities will reflect departmental needs and the successful candidate’s areas of expertise. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements The successful candidate will have a master’s degree or equivalent professional experience in a relevant field. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preference will be given to candidates who hold a D.M.A., Ph.D., or equivalent professional experience. Evidence of successful teaching at the university level preferred. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions A cover letter, curriculum vitae, three links to recent recordings demonstrating the applicant’s vocal and/or musical productions, with recordings preferably from the past five years, and the names and contact information for four references. The committee may solicit additional materials including letters of recommendation, sample teaching materials and/or evaluations, a sample syllabus, and a teaching statement that addresses pedagogical strategies candidates might use in a public university setting where students reflect the varied socioeconomic, racial, religious, and other demographics of the state. Application review will begin on November 9, 2026. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326200 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title LaToya Andriel Lain - Associate Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email lalain@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326334": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Teaching Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Teaching Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Biomedical Engineering-UG - 319300 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Deadline 11/05/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Teaching Assistant Professor Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0006136 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on Experience or Dependent on Qualifications. Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Lampe UNC - NCSU Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering stresses the application of science and engineering, mathematical analysis, and computer techniques to biomedical problems. The research and entrepreneurship of the faculty, students, and staff aim to accumulate, generate, and disseminate biomedical engineering knowledge to improve health care for the benefit of the people of North Carolina, the nation, and the world. Position Summary The Lampe UNC /NC State Joint Department of Biomedical Engineering is seeking applicants for a Teaching Assistant Professor in any area related to department specializations with priority given to bioinstrumentation, biomechanics and biologics-based design. This is a professional track faculty position with a focus on teaching and education. Responsibilities include but not limited to: -Delivery of lectures that cover the course objectives as stated on the course syllabus following the dates of the University of North Carolina-Chapel Hill and NC State University calendars for the given semester. -Assessment of student performance including exams, projects, laboratory assignments and/or homework assignments as outlined on the course syllabus. -If the course contains a lab section, overseeing the laboratory component to guarantee appropriate content of lab exercises and coordination of the lab with the lecture. -All other responsibilities associated with teaching the course including grading exams, papers and projects in a timely manner and providing help to students during scheduled office hours. -If a teaching assistant is provided, provide supervision to the teaching assistant and coordinate assignments not exceeding the workload of the teaching assistant. -The instructional load for this position will be 2 to 3 courses per semester for a total of 4 to 6 courses taught each academic year. Employment will be through UNC -Chapel Hill, but some courses may be taught on the NC State campus. -The individual must work productively and in a collaborative manner across all constituent BME entities, i.e. University of North Carolina College of Arts and Sciences, University of North Carolina School of Medicine and the NC State University College of Engineering. The Assistant Teaching Professor will conduct service in areas of need. This may include mentoring students or student organizations, developing study abroad programs, participating in assessment activities, curriculum development and/or academic advising. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in Biomedical Engineering, or related field. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Teaching experience. Engagement is the scholarship of teaching and learning. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326189 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Samantha Caudill, Human Resources Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email Samantha_Caudill@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree/degree level? Masters PharmaD DNP PhD JD MLS/MIS DVM DDS MD Other How did you find out about the position opening? CareerBuilder.com Monster.com Employment Security Commission UNC General Administration Job Board Indeed.com Chronicle of Higher Education Higheredjobs.com Job Fair Journal of Blacks in Higher Education Personal Referral Society of Human Resources Mgmt (SHRM) Trianglejobs.com UNC Online Job Posting Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
