ange of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Department of Chemistry at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is a nationally recognized leader in chemical education and research, with a mission to advance scientific discovery, educate future scientists, and serve the broader scientific community. As one of the largest and most research-intensive departments in the College of Arts and Sciences, the Department supports a vibrant academic community that includes faculty, staff, graduate students, postdoctoral scholars, and undergraduate majors. The Department delivers a comprehensive educational program that provides instruction to thousands of students annually through classroom and laboratory courses while fostering excellence in undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral training. Faculty members are deeply engaged in both teaching and mentoring and lead internationally recognized research programs spanning the chemical sciences. Research within the Department is supported by a broad portfolio of federal and private funding sources and encompasses fundamental and applied investigations that address important scientific and societal challenges. Housed across multiple research and instructional facilities, the Department maintains a dynamic environment that promotes interdisciplinary collaboration, innovation, and the generation of new knowledge. Position Summary The Department of Chemistry at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in analytical chemistry, broadly defined. We welcome candidates whose research advances the frontiers of measurement science and who are committed to building a nationally and internationally recognized research program. The successful candidate will pursue innovative scholarship, mentor students and trainees, and provide outstanding instruction at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Faculty responsibilities include contributing to curriculum innovation, participating in departmental and university service, and fostering a collaborative and inclusive academic community. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements * Ph.D. in Analytical Chemistry or a closely related field. * Significant research experience beyond the doctoral degree, typically including postdoctoral training. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience * Record of scholarly achievement and evidence of the potential to establish an innovative, externally funded research program. * Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring students from diverse backgrounds. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Please name each of the files listed below using the following nomenclature: “Applicant Last Name_Position #/VacancyID_File Descriptor.pdf” For example: “Smith_FAC0006055_Resume.pdf” Please only submit .pdf files. Required: Cover Letter (two pages max) CV/Resume List of References (with phone and email contact, one page) Research Statement (6 pages max, excluding references) Teaching Philosophy and Experience (one page) Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326266 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Search Committee Chair Department Contact Telephone or Email chemsearch@unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter List of References Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
