    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326268": {
      "title": "Chair, Department of Radiology",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Chair, Department of Radiology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Chair, Department of Radiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Med Ad-Deans Office - 420104 Posting Open Date 09/01/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Chair, Department of Radiology Appointment Type Admin Appointment with Faculty Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006074 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The School of Medicine at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill seeks an accomplished, collaborative, and visionary leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Radiology. This recruitment is Open Track/Open Rank, and the appropriate track and rank will be determined once the top candidate is selected. Aligned with the mission of the UNC School of Medicine, the Department of Radiology is committed to improving the health and well-being of the people of North Carolina and beyond through excellence in patient care, education, and research. UNC Radiology brings together outstanding clinical and research faculty, trainees, advanced practice providers, and professional staff across the full spectrum of diagnostic imaging, image-guided interventions, and radiological sciences. The Department combines the strengths of a leading academic department with the reach and opportunities of a growing health system, providing specialized imaging and interventional services across academic, hospital, ambulatory, and community settings. The Chair will provide strategic leadership across the Department’s clinical, educational, research, and administrative missions and will advance a shared vision for the future of UNC Radiology. The Chair will promote exceptional and compassionate patient care, educational excellence, scientific discovery and innovation, and the continued development of a nationally recognized academic Department. The Chair will recruit, develop, and retain outstanding faculty and leaders; foster a collaborative and high-performing culture; and ensure responsible stewardship of the Department’s financial, human, technological, and institutional resources. Working in close partnership with the School of Medicine, UNC Faculty Physicians, UNC Health, and University leadership, the Chair will advance an integrated approach to imaging and image-guided care and position the Department to respond to evolving patient needs, workforce challenges, technological advances, and changes in healthcare delivery. The Chair will foster interdisciplinary collaboration, strengthen the Department’s research and educational programs, and identify opportunities for strategic growth and innovation across the academic and clinical enterprise. As a senior institutional leader, the Chair will build strong relationships across organizational and disciplinary boundaries, contribute to broader School of Medicine and UNC Health priorities, and serve as a visible ambassador for UNC Radiology. The Chair will strengthen the Department’s reputation and impact locally, regionally, nationally, and internationally while fostering a culture grounded in excellence, collaboration, compassion, professionalism, and respect. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD, DO, or equivalent medical degree. Board certification in Diagnostic Radiology, Interventional Radiology, or an appropriate Radiology specialty by the American Board of Radiology or equivalent certifying organization. Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of North Carolina. Academic credentials and accomplishments appropriate for appointment at the rank of Professor in the University of North Carolina School of Medicine. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preference will be given to candidates with: A nationally recognized record of leadership and academic accomplishment in Radiology. Significant leadership experience within a large academic Department of Radiology or integrated imaging enterprise. Experience leading clinical growth, transformation, or integration across multiple sites or care settings. Demonstrated success developing innovative clinical programs and adapting care-delivery models in response to workforce, access, capacity, and operational challenges. Experience growing research programs, supporting extramural funding, developing research infrastructure, and fostering interdisciplinary and translational collaboration. Experience advancing educational programs and supporting innovation across undergraduate, graduate, and continuing medical education. Experience overseeing or partnering around major imaging technology, infrastructure, or capital investments. Understanding of emerging technologies and their implications for Radiology, including artificial intelligence, advanced analytics, and evolving imaging and image-guided therapies. Experience leading effectively within a matrixed environment requiring partnership among academic, faculty practice, hospital, and health-system leadership. Demonstrated success in faculty recruitment, retention, mentorship, succession planning, and leadership development. Experience with philanthropy, alumni engagement, and external partnerships supporting academic missions. Evidence of national leadership and engagement within Radiology or related professional organizations. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324731 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Jayne Ashby Department Contact Telephone or Email Jayne_Ashby@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Equal Employment Opportunity office at (919) 966-3576 or send an email to equalopportunity@unc.edu. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326249": {
      "title": "Pediatric Cardiologist",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Pediatric Cardiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Pediatric Cardiologist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Peds-Cardiology - 412003 Posting Open Date 03/15/2024 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Pediatric Cardiologist Appointment Type Fixed Term Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0005001 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 08/01/2024 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC School of Medicine has a rich tradition of excellence and care. Our mission is to improve the health and wellbeing of North Carolinians, and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. We strive to promote faculty, staff, and learner development in a diverse, respectful environment where our colleagues demonstrate professionalism, enhance learning, and create personal and professional sustainability. We optimize our partnership with the UNC Health System through close collaboration and commitment to service. OUR VISION Our vision is to be the nation’s leading public school of medicine. We are ranked 2nd in primary care education among all US schools of medicine and 5th among public peers in NIH research funding. Our Allied Health Department is home to five top-ranked divisions, and we are home to 18 top-ranked clinical and basic science departments in NIH research funding. OUR MISSION Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education, and research. Patient Care: We will promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We will prepare tomorrow’s health care professionals and biomedical researchers by facilitating learning within innovative curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education. We will cultivate outstanding teaching and research faculty, and we will recruit outstanding students and trainees from highly diverse backgrounds to create a socially responsible, highly skilled workforce. Research: We will develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers, and resources. We will provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our University to support outstanding research. We will foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic, and population research. Position Summary The Department of Pediatrics at the University of North Carolina School of Medicine is recruiting for an open rank, fixed term clinical faculty position for the Division of Pediatric Cardiology. We are seeking a faculty member to join our growing Division to augment our team of non-invasive cardiologists in the expansion of subspecialty services. Primary responsibilities will include interpretation of non-invasive imaging, outreach and telemedicine, and inpatient care. Individuals with expertise in transesophageal imaging for surgical or catheterization interventions and/or advanced imaging experience are encouraged. Clinical research and quality improvement interests will be fostered. The faculty member will be involved in the educational mission of the School of Medicine. As a top-tier academic medical center, UNC Children’s upholds a four-tiered mission to ‘ CARE ,’ aligning clinical care, advocacy, research, and education to deliver world-class family-centered care. The North Carolina Children’s Hospital is the clinical home of UNC Children’s. Our multidisciplinary experts work in satellite clinics across the state and deliver state of the art tertiary care at UNC Children’s. The Triangle area of Raleigh/Durham/Chapel Hill is consistently ranked among the nation’s best places to live. The region offers affordable living, a temperate climate, easy access to beach and mountains, vibrant dining and cultural offerings. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements The candidate must be board eligible / certified in Pediatric Cardiology Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience The ideal candidate should also be skilled and interested in the practice of ambulatory and inpatient pediatric cardiology. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/276617 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Timothy Hoffman, MD Department Contact Telephone or Email thoffman@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other * Are you Board Certified or Board Eligible in Pediatric Cardiology? Yes No * Please describe your experience working with an academic training program involving medical students, graduate students, residents or other similar programs? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326247": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Medicine-Hematology - 411490 Posting Open Date 09/30/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006133 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow`s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary The Division of Hematology in the Department of Medicine at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is recruiting a faculty member interested in clinical research or clinician educator positions focused on the management of patients with acute leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes. This candidate will be expected to work with a group of faculty and APPs in the management of patients with acute leukemia, myelodysplastic syndromes and MDS /myeloproliferative neoplasms. This candidate will participate in a robust and active inpatient and outpatient clinical research program in Leukemia at the University of North Carolina. The responsibilities include attending on the inpatient hematologic malignancy service and managing patients with acute leukemia and MDS in the outpatient clinics at the University of North Carolina or our affiliated Cancer Centers. As this is an open rank posting, academic rank and track will be determined by the candidate’s experience and achievements. This position can be fixed term, tenure track or variable track. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD, MD/PhD, DO or MBBS degrees. All individuals will have completed a fellowship in adult hematology and/or oncology and be board eligible/certified in hematology and/or oncology. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience The preferred individual will have at least three years of experience managing patients with acute leukemia and myelodysplastic syndromes, and a history of leading clinical research studies for this patient population. They will have a history of working collaboratively in an academic medical setting and mentoring hematology/oncology trainees. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326196 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Shelby Abbott-Lunsford, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email shelby_abbott-lunsford@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/326227": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please use the Research Statement option to upload research, teaching, and service statements as a combined pdf. Please include names and contact information for three letters of reference with the application. A fourth letter will be requested upon interview invitation. Please use the Writing/Research Sample option to upload up to three published papers or preprints of your work. Posting Information Posting Information Department Psychology and Neuroscience - 319100 Posting Open Date 09/29/2026 Application Deadline 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Assistant Professor Appointment Type Tenured/Tenure Track Vacancy ID FAC0006130 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Commensurate with Education and Experience Proposed Start Date 07/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! The Department of Psychology and Neuroscience at the University of North Carolina ( UNC ) at Chapel Hill invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor level in the field of Behavioral and Integrative Neuroscience, with appointments to begin July 2027. We seek outstanding candidates in each of the following areas: (1) Human Neuroscience of Substance Use Disorders. We seek candidates conducting human-subjects research focused on the neural mechanisms of substance use disorders. Relevant research may address risk factors, development, maintenance, recovery, and treatment. Relevant approaches may include neuroimaging, computational modeling, functional neural network analyses, fNIRS, EEG / ERP , noninvasive brain stimulation, machine learning approaches or other related methodologies that provide mechanistic insight to advance our understanding of substance use disorders. (2) Pre-Clinical Neuroscience of Substance Use Disorders. We seek candidates investigating the neural and cellular mechanisms underlying substance use disorders using pre-clinical animal models. Relevant approaches include, but are not limited to, circuit, cellular, molecular, and systems neuroscience approaches, as well as the integration of emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence, computational methods, New Approach Methodologies (NAMs), human iPSC-derived neural systems or organoids, and advanced behavioral and physiological analyses. Successful applicants will join the Behavioral and Integrative Neuroscience program within the Department of Psychology and Neuroscience, which has longstanding strengths in the neurobiology of reward, addiction, and motivated behavior and a collaborative research environment including the UNC Bowles Center for Alcohol Studies, the UNC Neuroscience Center, the Biomedical Research Imaging Center, the School of Medicine, and other programs across campus. Candidates who leverage innovative computational, methodological and quantitative, approaches to address questions related to alcohol and substance use disorders are especially encouraged to apply. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The primary purpose of the Psychology and Neuroscience Department is to provide excellent education, research and service in the field. This goal breaks down into four important components: 1) to teach psychology and neuroscience to undergraduates in a manner that will introduce them vigorously to its broad scope; 2) to offer scientific and professional training to graduate students in the areas of behavioral and integrative neuroscience, clinical, cognitive, developmental, quantitative, and social psychology; 3) to carry out cutting-edge research in these areas, and 4) to provide consulting and administrative support services to the science and profession of psychology as well as to the university, the community, the state, and the nation. The Department consists of six programs: behavioral and integrative neuroscience; clinical psychology; cognitive psychology; developmental psychology; quantitative psychology, and social psychology. Each program is designed to acquaint the student thoroughly with the theoretical and research content of the specialty and to provide training in the research skills needed to become a competent and creative investigator. In addition, the programs focus on the development of appropriate professional skills. The Department of Psychology and Neuroscience currently ranks 2nd in the College in grant funding with over $15 million annually in awarded grants and approximately $20 million annually in expenditures from all funds. The Department of Psychology and Neuroscience has the largest undergraduate major in the College of Arts and Sciences with approximately 1900 majors, and one of the largest graduate Ph.D. programs with approximately 130 graduate students. The Department is also home to the UNC Psychology and Neuroscience Community Clinic, which provides therapeutic treatment and assessment services to a variety of constituencies on campus and in the community. Position Summary The primary purpose of the Department of Psychology and Neuroscience is to provide excellent education, research and service in the field. This goal breaks down into four important components: 1) to teach psychology and neuroscience to undergraduates in a manner that will introduce them vigorously to its broad scope; 2) to offer scientific and professional training to graduate students in the areas of behavioral and integrative neuroscience, clinical, cognitive, developmental, quantitative, and social psychology; 3) to carry out cutting-edge research in these areas, and 4) to provide consulting and administrative support services to the science and profession of psychology and neuroscience as well as to the university, the community, the state, and the nation. The Department consists of six programs: behavioral and integrative neuroscience; clinical psychology; cognitive psychology; developmental psychology; quantitative psychology, and social psychology. Each program is designed to acquaint the student thoroughly with the theoretical and research content of the specialty and to provide training in the research skills needed to become a competent and creative investigator. In addition, the programs focus on the development of appropriate professional skills. The Department of Psychology and Neuroscience currently ranks 2nd in the College in grant funding with over $12 million annually in awarded grants and approximately $20 million annually in expenditures from all funds. The department has two large undergraduate majors (Psychology and Neuroscience) in the College of Arts and Sciences with approximately 2900 total majors, a minor in Neuroscience and one of the largest graduate Ph.D. programs with approximately 120 graduate students. The Department is also home to the UNC Psychology and Neuroscience Community Clinic, which provides therapeutic treatment and assessment services to a variety of constituencies on campus and in the community. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements PhD in the areas of Psychology, Neuroscience, or a related field is required. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience We seek candidates with an excellent record of research productivity, the potential to develop an independent, externally funded, and interdisciplinary research program, and a commitment to teaching and mentorship at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Please use the Research Statement option to upload research, teaching, and service statements as a combined pdf. Please include names and contact information for three letters of reference with the application. A fourth letter will be requested upon interview invitation. Please use the Writing/Research Sample option to upload up to three published papers or preprints of your work. Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325922 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Sylvia Fitting, Professor Department Contact Telephone or Email sfitting@email.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Writing/research Sample Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
