    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325033": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Radiology - VascularIntervntnl - 412803 Posting Open Date 08/21/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006062 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary Position Description The Department of Radiology at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking a full time, fellowship trained Interventional Radiologist to join the Interventional Radiology Division. This position supports the department’s clinical, educational, and academic missions within a high volume, tertiary care academic medical center. The Interventional Radiology Division performs a broad range of vascular and non-vascular procedures and provides CTA and MRA interpretation. Divisional clinical strengths include interventional oncology, treatment of vascular malformations, portal hypertension, venous disease interventions, women’s health, and solid organ transplant-related interventions. The division maintains an independent outpatient clinic, an inpatient admitting service, and provides procedural services for a local outpatient dialysis access center. Clinical care is delivered across multiple state of the art locations, including nine interventional procedure suites with a 16 bed pre and post procedure holding area at UNC Memorial Hospital in Chapel Hill, two interventional procedure suites with a nine bed holding area at Hillsborough Hospital, onsite Interventional Radiology services at UNC Health Johnston locations in Smithfield and Clayton supporting both inpatient and outpatient populations, and an office based laboratory in Chapel Hill. The division supports comprehensive training for Integrated Interventional Radiology, Independent Interventional Radiology, and Diagnostic Radiology residents through a high procedural case volume. Position Responsibilities Perform image guided vascular and non vascular interventional radiology procedures using ultrasound, fluoroscopy, and CT guidance Provide clinical care across inpatient, outpatient clinic, admitting service, dialysis access, and office based laboratory settings Interpret CTA and MRA studies as part of the clinical service Perform a wide range of interventional procedures, which may include image guided biopsies; venous access procedures; thermal tumor ablation (microwave and cryoablation); chemoembolization and radioembolization; vertebroplasty and kyphoplasty; uterine artery embolization; prostatic artery embolization; and endovenous ablation procedures Participate in the education and supervision of Integrated IR, Independent IR, and Diagnostic Radiology residents Collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical teams across medical and surgical specialties Participate in quality improvement, scholarly, or research activities consistent with departmental needs Appointment Details This is an open rank, fixed term faculty appointment at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Flexible work arrangements, including virtual and hybrid work locations, are an integral part of the School of Medicine’s Working Forward initiative. This position may be eligible for a virtual or hybrid work arrangement, in accordance with UNC policy and subject to approval based on the unit’s business needs. Please note that the approved work location may change over time to meet operational requirements. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Board certified or board eligible Radiologist Fellowship training in Interventional Radiology or equivalent clinical experience Demonstrated ability to perform a broad range of vascular and non vascular interventional procedures Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary clinical teams Interest or experience in resident education within an academic medical setting Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/324277 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Alexis Evans, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email alexis_evans@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/325031": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department Radiology - Chest - 412805 Posting Open Date 08/13/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0006054 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 11/02/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local child care centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit Our mission is to improve the health and well-being of North Carolinians and others whom we serve. We accomplish this by providing leadership and excellence in the interrelated areas of patient care, education and research. Patient care: We promote health and provide superb clinical care while maintaining our strong tradition of reaching underserved populations and reducing health disparities across North Carolina and beyond. Education: We prepare tomorrow’s healthcare professionals and biomedical researchers from all backgrounds by facilitating learning within innovative and integrated curricula and team-oriented interprofessional education to ensure a highly skilled workforce. Research: We develop and support a rich array of outstanding health sciences research programs, centers and resources. We provide infrastructure and opportunities for collaboration among disciplines throughout and beyond our university to support outstanding research. We foster programs in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic and population research. Position Summary Position Description The Department of Radiology at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill is seeking a Cardiothoracic Radiologist to join the Cardiothoracic Imaging Division. This position supports the clinical, educational, and collaborative missions of the department within a high volume academic medical center. The Cardiothoracic Imaging Division is staffed by radiologists with specialized expertise in cardiovascular and thoracic imaging. The division is responsible for interpretation of portable and conventional chest radiographs, thoracic computed tomography (CT) examinations, cardiac CT and MRI studies, and the performance of chest fluoroscopy. The service functions in close collaboration with pulmonology, oncology, internal medicine, cardiology, and cardiac and thoracic surgical services. The division also performs image-guided thoracic procedures, including CT-guided lung and mediastinal biopsies, with opportunities for interested faculty to participate in procedural practice. Division faculty participate as integral members of the Multidisciplinary Thoracic Oncology and Interstitial Lung Disease programs and contribute imaging expertise to coordinated diagnostic evaluation and treatment planning. Faculty are also involved in education and academic activities across the department. Position Responsibilities Interpret cardiothoracic imaging studies, including chest radiographs, thoracic CT, and cardiac CT and MRI studies Perform and/or supervise chest fluoroscopy as part of the clinical service Participate in multidisciplinary clinical care through collaboration with pulmonology, oncology, cardiology, internal medicine, and cardiac and thoracic surgical services Contribute imaging expertise to multidisciplinary conferences and programs, including the Multidisciplinary Thoracic Oncology Program Teach and mentor diagnostic radiology residents, chest imaging fellows, and medical students Participate in quality improvement, scholarly, or academic activities consistent with departmental needs Appointment Details This is an open rank, fixed term faculty appointment at the rank of Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements MD or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Board certified or board eligible in Diagnostic Radiology, or eligible for equivalent certification pathways acceptable for faculty appointment and clinical practice. Fellowship training in Cardiothoracic Imaging or equivalent clinical experience. Eligibility for medical licensure in the State of North Carolina. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary clinical teams. Interest or experience in resident and fellow education in an academic medical setting. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/323327 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Alexis Evans, HR Consultant Department Contact Telephone or Email alexis_evans@med.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
