    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/321864": {
      "title": "Cornea &amp; External Disease (Open Rank Faculty)",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Cornea &amp; External Disease (Open Rank Faculty) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Cornea & External Disease (Open Rank Faculty) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Individuals wishing to be considered must submit a formal application at the UNC Jobsite at the following link: https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/314975. In addition to a formal application, candidates must submit a CV, cover letter, and list of at least 3 individuals (to include contact information and email address) who may be contacted to provide a professional reference. Posting Information Posting Information Department Ophthalmology - 413201 Posting Open Date 03/20/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Cornea & External Disease (Open Rank Faculty) Appointment Type Open Rank Vacancy ID FAC0005861 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Proposed Start Date 10/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class medical care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous