    "https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319134": {
      "title": "Open Rank",
      "description": "UNC-Chapel Hill Employment Opportunities | Open Rank Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Careers At Carolina Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Working at Carolina Open Rank Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Department ASOD Operative Dentistry - 436520 Posting Open Date 05/18/2026 Application Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Position Type Permanent Faculty Working Title Open Rank Appointment Type Faculty Vacancy ID FAC0005936 Full-time/Part-time Full-Time Permanent Hours per week 40 FTE 1 Position Location North Carolina, US Hiring Range Dependent on qualifications Proposed Start Date 09/01/2026 Position Information Be a Tar Heel! A global higher education leader in innovative teaching, research and public service, the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill consistently ranks as one of the nation’s top public universities . Known for its beautiful campus, world-class health care, commitment to the arts and top athletic programs, Carolina is an ideal place to teach, work and learn. One of the best college towns and best places to live in the United States, Chapel Hill has diverse social, cultural, recreation and professional opportunities that span the campus and community. University employees can choose from a wide range of professional training opportunities for career growth, skill development and lifelong learning and enjoy exclusive perks for numerous retail, restaurant and performing arts discounts, savings on local childcare centers and special rates on select campus events. UNC -Chapel Hill offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package , paid leave, and a variety of health, life and retirement plans and additional programs that support a healthy work/life balance. The Adams School of Dentistry, established in 1950 and made possible by an Act of the North Carolina General Assembly in 1949, is now part of a dynamic Health Science campus! The school provides oral health care to more than 90,000 patients each year! With more than 6,400 living alumni in 27 nations and all 50 states, the school’s impact to oral health in North Carolina, throughout the U.S., and around the world is unprecedented. Adams School of Dentistry is at the forefront of oral health care, education, research, and leadership. We are building on 75 years of high-quality patient care, an evolving academic learning environment, cutting-edge research across a spectrum of science and a culture where all belong. We lead the way in oral health care and education with compassion and sensitivity, and we are committed to caring for rural and underserved populations across NC and beyond. The Adams School of Dentistry is one of six health science schools (Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Social Work, Public Health) at the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill and is the first dental school in the state of North Carolina. The ASOD consists of seven (7) Academic Departments: Biomedical Sciences , Craniofacial and Surgical Care (Craniofacial Center, Geriatrics/Special Care, Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery, and Oral Medicine), Restorative Sciences (General Dentistry, Operative & Biomaterials and Prosthodontics), Pediatric Dentistry and Dental Public Health , Orthodontics , Diagnostic Sciences (Oral Microbiology, Orofacial Pain/Sleep, Pathology and Radiology) and Periodontology, Endodontics and Dental Hygiene (one department). It is an exciting time to join the Adams School of Dentistry as we have finalized a new strategic plan and have embarked on exciting team initiatives! Our Motto : Extraordinary people. Exemplary scholarship. Exceptional care. Our Mission : To educate and empower the next generation of leaders in oral health care through excellence in education, research, patient care, and service, demonstrating responsible stewardship of our profession. We serve the people of North Carolina and beyond and strive for global impact. Our Vision : To serve as the leader for oral health care professionals through our innovative curriculum, interdisciplinary research, and commitment to collaborative patient care. Our Values : Integrity: We engage authentically, ethically, and honestly, cultivating an environment of trust and respect. Curiosity: We celebrate discovery and innovation, embracing opportunities for growth, seeking creative solutions, and seizing new possibilities. Collaboration: We value teamwork, recognizing our individual and collective efforts and advocating for the well-being and success of our people and the communities we serve. Belonging: We honor our unique perspectives, dedicated to creating a fair, accessible, and inclusive environment where everyone feels valued and supported. Adams School of Dentistry Strategic Plan – UNC School of Dentistry #uncdentistry #growingcareers #dentalcareers #dentaljobs Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The UNC Adams School of Dentistry Division of Comprehensive Oral Health houses several disciplines including, Periodontology, Dental Hygiene, Comprehensive Dentistry, Operative Dentistry/BioMaterials, Prosthodontics, and Endodontics. The Operative discipline focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and prognosis of defects of the teeth that do not require full coverage restorations for correction. Position Summary The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill Adams School of Dentistry invites applications for a full-time, open rank faculty member in Operative, Cariology and Biomaterials Dentistry, Department of Restorative Sciences. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, assuring safe and effective delivery of patient care, providing didactic and clinical education, course and curriculum leadership, summative and formative student assessment and leading small group seminars. The successful candidate will be expected to participate in teaching at the pre-doctoral and graduate levels; collaborate with pre-doctoral and graduate program directors on the creative design and implementation of ongoing interactive curriculum; participate in duties consistent with school and university requirements for performance and scholarship; and participate in the UNC Adams School of Dentistry Dental Faculty Practice. The position also offers continuing education and professional service. Primary Responsibilities Teaching and Education Teach predoctoral and/or graduate courses in operative dentistry, cariology, preventive dentistry, and dental biomaterial Supervise and mentor students and residents in clinical operative dentistry and general dentistry Participate in curriculum development, assessment, and continuous quality improvement Integrate contemporary concepts such as minimally invasive dentistry, caries risk assessment, and biomaterials science into teaching Mentor students, residents, and junior faculty as appropriate to rank Clinical Practice Provide patient care in operative, esthetic dentistry and general dentistry consistent with institutional standards Supervise clinical care in student and resident clinics Promote evidence-based, patient-centered, and preventive approaches to oral health care Research and Scholarship Participate and lead scholarly activity in cariology, dental materials, restorative dentistry, or related fields Publish in peer-reviewed journals and present at national and international meetings Pursue extramural research funding, as appropriate to rank and track when applicable Collaborate within the institution and across disciplines (e.g., materials science, biomedical engineering, public health) Service and Leadership Participate in departmental, school, and university service activities Contribute to professional organizations at the local, national, or international level Support accreditation, faculty governance, and institutional initiatives Minimum Education and Experience Requirements DDS , DMD , or equivalent dental degree from an accredited institution Completion of advanced training or demonstrated expertise in operative dentistry, cariology, or dental biomaterials Be Eligible for NC Dental or Instructor’s License Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Preferences include considerable experience in educating dental students in preclinical and/or clinical settings or considerable experience in private general practice, or completion of an advanced dental education program; demonstrated excellent clinical credentials; supervisory, organizational, mentoring, customer service, written and verbal communication skills, and a strong background in all aspects of general, operative and esthetic dentistry. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities This position is designated as a Campus Security Authority in accordance with the Clery Act. This position will be required to report Clery crimes to the Clery Compliance Manager and complete annual training about reporting responsibilities. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/319010 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Dr. Ibrahim Duqum, Department Chair Department Contact Telephone or Email duqumi@dentistry.unc.edu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Certification/licenses List of References Degree Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Teaching Philosophy/evaluations Other Document 2 Other Document 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
