in the areas of basic, translational, mechanistic, and population research. Position Summary The UNC Department of Emergency Medicine is seeking a Psychiatrist to join our Division of Acute Psychiatry. This clinician will provide clinical services in the Behavioral Health Emergency Department and will lead a team of experienced and engaged advanced practice providers and licensed clinical social workers. This is a full-time fixed term (clinical) position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. The rank will be based on the qualifications of the applicants. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements Medical Doctor (M.D.) degree or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (D.O.) degree. Preferred Qualifications, Competencies, and Experience Strong clinical skills and demonstrated administrative and clinical efficiency skills necessary to enable them to successfully provide clinical, supervisory, and educational services. Clinical experience working with patients of all ages. Special Physical/Mental Requirements Campus Security Authority Responsibilities Not Applicable. Special Instructions Quick Link https://unc.peopleadmin.com/postings/262540 Department Contact Information Department Contact Name and Title Kelly Armstrong Department Contact Telephone or Email kelly_armstrong@med.unc.eu Academic Personnel Office Contact Information If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the University’s Executive Vice Chancellor and Provost office at (919)-962-1091 or send an email to facultyrecruitment@unc.edu. Please note: The Executive Vice Chancellor & Provost office will not be able to provide specific updates regarding position or application status. If you have any questions about the job requirements or the hiring department notify the Department Contact. Equal Opportunity Employer Statement The University is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes all to apply without regard to age, color, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or sexual orientation. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae / Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest degree? PhD MD PharmD DDS DVM JD MLS/MIS Masters Other Office of Human Resources 919-843-2300 hr@unc.edu © 2026 The University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill About Human Resources UNC-Chapel Hill Policies Office of Faculty Affairs To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
